{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote","id":1133616,"title":"Remote Sniper Rote","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-24T18:23:48-07:00","id":1133616,"title":"Remote Sniper Rote","content":"So I'm curious as to what you guys think of this, and it's vulgarity.<br /> <br /> A Matter 2/Correspondence 3 rote.<br /> <br /> You create a portal and shoot through it. Depending on circumstances I would say this is USUALLY coincidental, as snipers with high powered rifles really could basically appear bullets out of thin air as far as the target is concerned, but certain environments and firing angles could MAKE it highly vulgar. A bullet dropping from directly above or below the target for example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T18:50:14-07:00","id":1133621,"title":"","content":"If it's in range where a sniper shot could be made and the environment is such that it's believable, well someone could be channeling Tom Berenger's character in Sniper or Mark Wahlberg in the movie version of Shooter. Given the prevalence of amazing archers in fantasy fiction and movies, some others might be able to justify remote bow sniping at certain ranges.<br /> <br /> Coincidental or vulgar magick would depend on the desired effect and how observers would see it. If the observers play the game <i>Car Wars</i>, then you can get pretty vulgar if shooting a car. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T18:58:56-07:00","id":1133622,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't that just be Matter 2 / Correspondence 2? Or is this something M20 changed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T19:26:30-07:00","id":1133631,"title":"","content":"This seems a bit unnecessary. If you're going to keep this coincidental, there's no big advantage to shooting through a portal. Either you have a viable if improbable shot you can can boost easily, or you're doing something like ricochet shots (which is Corr 2/Force 2 IIRC from Rev and nothing in M20 seems to have changed that). Actually shooting a bullet through a portal only makes sense to shoot someone you couldn't actually hit, which is going to get vulgar pretty fast (even if w/o witnesses), and seems an odd choice of tactics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T07:27:28-07:00","id":1133782,"title":"","content":"You could use a portal to shoot someone that's on the other side of the planet. That you can't do with Forces nor boosts. It's not a horrendus tactic if you were spying someone trough Correspondence, and now you need to kill him.<br /> <br /> Would this be Vulgar?. in M20 the hypotetical observer isn't omniscient, he can't know that YOU made the shoot, he only knows that someone was killed by a bullet that come out of &quot;nowhere&quot;, if the target is in the open, I think it would be Coincident (surely there was a sniper somewhere), otherwise it would be Vulgar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-25-2017, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:21:25-07:00","id":1133946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1133782#post1133782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could use a portal to shoot someone that's on the other side of the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I could use magic to give someone an aneurysm on the other side of the planet that wouldn't cause any of the questions a gunshot would. A bullet killing someone is a bullet that can be traced without magic (meaning you need to take further steps to avoid that), and of course, gun damage is far less reliable than magic damage. So if we're killing people outside of a direct line of sight and past what a sniper rifle can effectively manage... why bother with the rifle at all?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would this be Vulgar?. in M20 the hypotetical observer isn't omniscient, he can't know that YOU made the shoot, he only knows that someone was killed by a bullet that come out of &quot;nowhere&quot;, if the target is in the open, I think it would be Coincident (surely there was a sniper somewhere), otherwise it would be Vulgar </div> </div> </div>The HAP isn't just at one side of a Correspondence portal. The HAP watching you shoot a rifle into a portal in space notices the extremely vulgar portal in space that you're aiming and shooting through.<br /> <br /> If I use Life and Prime to create a tiger out of nothing at a zoo, it's vulgar despite most people assuming the tiger running around just escaped a pen. The HAP notices me conjuring a tiger out of thin air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T14:34:47-07:00","id":1133949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1133946#post1133946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I could use magic to give someone an aneurysm on the other side of the planet that wouldn't cause any of the questions a gunshot would. A bullet killing someone is a bullet that can be traced without magic (meaning you need to take further steps to avoid that), and of course, gun damage is far less reliable than magic damage. So if we're killing people outside of a direct line of sight and past what a sniper rifle can effectively manage... why bother with the rifle at all?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The HAP isn't just at one side of a Correspondence portal. The HAP watching you shoot a rifle into a portal in space notices the extremely vulgar portal in space that you're aiming and shooting through.<br /> <br /> If I use Life and Prime to create a tiger out of nothing at a zoo, it's vulgar despite most people assuming the tiger running around just escaped a pen. The HAP notices me conjuring a tiger out of thin air.</div> </div> </div> </div>The HAP sees you shooting a gun. You don't see where the bullet lands, and presumes it missed the target. Another HAP sees somebody walking down the street get hit in the throat with a sniper round. And presumes there is a shooter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-25T23:06:05-07:00","id":1134060,"title":"","content":"If the portal isn't big enough for the HAP to see, how is it big enough for you to both aim and fire a rifle through it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T09:31:48-07:00","id":1134158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1134060#post1134060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the portal isn't big enough for the HAP to see, how is it big enough for you to both aim and fire a rifle through it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the portal making equipment is on the rifle and tuned to open the portal along the path of the bullet? No aiming necessary. Just a digital flick of the switch via Radio ADEI.<br /> <br /> The aiming/gun test is for how well you've aimed the portal. Not for litterally looking through a window sized hole in reality and shooting through it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T09:52:23-07:00","id":1134163,"title":"","content":"So... the HAP notices that your gun goes &quot;bang&quot; but there's no muzzle flash/etc. because all that follows the path of the barrel? Or the HAP that see where the bullet should impact and how it just vanishes and hits nothing? How, exactly, do you hit anything if you aren't actively aiming the gun? Are you tagging the target with the portal so that you now have to add Life to the spell to latch the effect to them (And again, at that point, why are we even bothering with a gun?).<br /> <br /> This feels like one of these discussions where vulgar without witnesses is being ignored to try to claim something is coincidental. Yes, part of the reason for HAP is to allow a contextual flexibility between coincidental and vulgar w/o witnesses, but no bullets get fired and then teleport somewhere else, and continue into a target. The HAP ruling isn't there to eliminate vulgar w/o witnesses, it's there to allow minor effects that would be vulgar under HOP to slide past to make the game fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T10:42:17-07:00","id":1134519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote#post1133616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm curious as to what you guys think of this, and it's vulgarity.<br /> <br /> A Matter 2/Correspondence 3 rote.<br /> <br /> You create a portal and shoot through it. Depending on circumstances I would say this is USUALLY coincidental, as snipers with high powered rifles really could basically appear bullets out of thin air as far as the target is concerned, but certain environments and firing angles could MAKE it highly vulgar. A bullet dropping from directly above or below the target for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still wondering why you need Matter at all and can't do this with Correspondence 2.<br /> <br /> I largely agree with Heavy. If it's something that could really happen, even if nearly impossible, it's Coincidental. A space-warp is outside that. To make this work Coincidentally, I'd say that it would probably work as a Correspondence 2/Forces 2 (for carefully managed ricochets) or Correspondence 2/Entropy 2 (for the &quot;lucky&quot; &quot;bounce&quot; version) effect and come off something like the sniper shot in the first episode of Alphas. (Both would really be fine with Correspondence 1, but the &quot;Sphere parity&quot; jumps it up a dot to being able to use Forces or Entropy). A very very careful set up might work with just Correspondence 1/Entropy 1 (knowing the exact layout between the shooter and target, and picking the ultimate optimal trajectory), but I'd probably say that's just a way to ease the Firearms roll significantly.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, any spacewarp version (which, since it's just moving around a bullet, why would it need more?) seems like it's automatically Correspondence 2 and one degree of Vulgar depending on the set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:43:07-07:00","id":1134574,"title":"","content":"Something fun you can do with sniper rifles at far ranges, is that with Corr 1/Entropy 1/Forces 1 you're firing at ranges where natural ballistics starts doing some crazy stuff without magic; if you can follow the right path through the local microclimates, the bullet's path with bend and curve. When you're talking about a target at the 1+ Km range, with enough distances between things, you can actually shoot people despite stuff being in between direct line of sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T06:58:06-07:00","id":1134821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I could use magic to give someone an aneurysm on the other side of the planet that wouldn't cause any of the questions a gunshot would. A bullet killing someone is a bullet that can be traced without magic (meaning you need to take further steps to avoid that), and of course, gun damage is far less reliable than magic damage. So if we're killing people outside of a direct line of sight and past what a sniper rifle can effectively manage... why bother with the rifle at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you don't have Life, but have a rifle and a paradigm that allows to use it as a focus?<br /> <br /> I grant it's not the best way, but sometimes you don't have access to the best way. Also, I would argue Mage isn't about finding the best way, but about flavor. I find a deadly supernatural sniper rifle that can get you no matter where you are to be very cool<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The HAP isn't just at one side of a Correspondence portal. The HAP watching you shoot a rifle into a portal in space notices the extremely vulgar portal in space that you're aiming and shooting through.<br /> <br /> If I use Life and Prime to create a tiger out of nothing at a zoo, it's vulgar despite most people assuming the tiger running around just escaped a pen. The HAP notices me conjuring a tiger out of thin air.<br /> .<br /> .<br /> .<br /> So... the HAP notices that your gun goes &quot;bang&quot; but there's no muzzle flash/etc. because all that follows the path of the barrel? Or the HAP that see where the bullet should impact and how it just vanishes and hits nothing? How, exactly, do you hit anything if you aren't actively aiming the gun? Are you tagging the target with the portal so that you now have to add Life to the spell to latch the effect to them (And again, at that point, why are we even bothering with a gun?). </div> </div> </div>You're making it seem more complicated than it really is: You don't need to open a literal hole in space where people can theoretically see trough, Correspondence it's just an excuse for the bullet to appear in the other side of the planet, the &quot;form&quot; of the spell it's dependant on Paradigm.<br /> <br /> If you shot with the rifle, the bullet get's teleported after leaving the barrel, and reapears at the other side of the planet (you were aiming with your correspondence googles/special targeting system), a person won't see anything because your rifle makes all sounds and everything related to the shoot (you shoot), and then the bullet can't be perceived by normal senses, it's too fast. If the observer can't find the bullet in your end, that's normal, because people do miss where things fall, the average observer hasn't knowledge of where did you shoot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">This feels like one of these discussions where vulgar without witnesses is being ignored to try to claim something is coincidental. Yes, part of the reason for HAP is to allow a contextual flexibility between coincidental and vulgar w/o witnesses, but no bullets get fired and then teleport somewhere else, and continue into a target. The HAP ruling isn't there to eliminate vulgar w/o witnesses, it's there to allow minor effects that would be vulgar under HOP to slide past to make the game fun.</span></span><br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I largely agree with Heavy. If it's something that could really happen, even if nearly impossible, it's Coincidental. A space-warp is outside that. To make this work Coincidentally, I'd say that it would probably work as a Correspondence 2/Forces 2 (for carefully managed ricochets) or Correspondence 2/Entropy 2 (for the &quot;lucky&quot; &quot;bounce&quot; version) effect and come off something like the sniper shot in the first episode of Alphas. (Both would really be fine with Correspondence 1, but the &quot;Sphere parity&quot; jumps it up a dot to being able to use Forces or Entropy). A very very careful set up might work with just Correspondence 1/Entropy 1 (knowing the exact layout between the shooter and target, and picking the ultimate optimal trajectory), but I'd probably say that's just a way to ease the Firearms roll significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>T<b>hat's not how things work, and to prove it I summon the most basic HAP example: <i>A coin appearing from nowhere in your pocket </i></b>(Corr 2 can do that): It's Coincident in HAP, the Observer it's not in your pocket. <b>End of story</b>, or it should be, as that was the example used to distinguish HAP from HOP, if my memory doesn't fail.<br /> <br /> The Observer Its Hypothetical because it's not a real witness and it's &quot;everywhere&quot;, but it's Average because it hasn't supernatural senses nor specialized mundane knowledge. The method its intended to determine if a thing it's Vulgar Without Witnesses.<br /> <br /> The general idea it's that something it's Coincident, if a person that was watching the whole scene with normal sense from a normal place can't discern anything weird, you can't obfuscate the scene conjuring darkness, nor teleporting the spell at the other side of the planet or anything like that (you can't &quot;blind&quot; the Observer, it always has it's normal senses), but at the same time the observer isn't a balistic expert that knows how guns work, and where a bullet should land, nor has superhuman senses to follow a bullet, see that it warps outside reality, and then reapears in the other side of the planet.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I would argue that the observer should be able to see a bullet changing it's direction mid air and failing to hit you when you use Forces to slightly deflect a shot. Bullets do not suddenly turn mid air that way. You wouldn't be able to make someone get an aneurism Coincidentally, because sickness isn't something that just *appears* in your body from nowhere, you healt at the time would be a factor that would determine Vulgarity. And so on.<br /> <br /> HAP does accept a level of goofyness that leaves things without explanation. You can't make a tiger appear in the zoo because a tiger it's big, and the observer should see it appearing from nowhere (barring obfuscations that would make the spell Vulgar Without Witnesses, like doing it in a closed space that's big enough to harbor a person), a coin appearing in your pocket, on the other hand it's Coincident (the most basic HAP example), and so it's a bullet appearing and blasting something, as bullets do when you're being sniped without your knowledge (if it &quot;lodges&quot; itself in your head without breaking your skull, then yeah, it's Vulgar with or without witnesses).<br /> <br /> I seem to remember that HAP critics used your very arguments to favor HOP. Are you two applying HOP?, because it would be useful to know if you're applying HOP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-28-2017, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:03:08-07:00","id":1134862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1134821#post1134821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you don't have Life, but have a rifle and a paradigm that allows to use it as a focus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever a mage's Focus is that allows them to use rifles as Instruments doesn't really matter to if the effect is coincidental or vulgar.<br /> <br /> And yes, sometimes your Sphere selection means you're stuck with a less effective method. Shooting someone across the world with Correspondence is less effective than just killing them directly because the rifle adds complications to how to do this. It's not impossible, it's just not a great way of doing things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I grant it's not the best way, but sometimes you don't have access to the best way. Also, I would argue Mage isn't about finding the best way, but about flavor. I find a deadly supernatural sniper rifle that can get you no matter where you are to be very cool. </div> </div> </div>Great. That also means sucking up the consequences that sometimes this is going to be vulgar magic because you're taking flavor over other considerations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're making it seem more complicated than it really is: You don't need to open a literal hole in space where people can theoretically see trough, Correspondence it's just an excuse for the bullet to appear in the other side of the planet, the &quot;form&quot; of the spell it's dependant on Paradigm. </div> </div> </div>The complexity is relevant and deserves discussion. As well, there's two distinct ways of handling this: teleporting the bullet and firing the rifle through a Correspondence window.<br /> <br /> The first is full of complications that still run afoul of potential vulgarity. The second is much easier, but overtly vulgar; the literal hole in space lets you aim and fire the weapon normally without any other magical considerations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you shot with the rifle, the bullet get's teleported after leaving the barrel, and reapears at the other side of the planet (you were aiming with your correspondence googles/special targeting system), a person won't see anything because your rifle makes all sounds and everything related to the shoot (you shoot), and then the bullet can't be perceived by normal senses, it's too fast. If the observer can't find the bullet in your end, that's normal, because people do miss where things fall, the average observer hasn't knowledge of where did you shoot. </div> </div> </div>OK, lets start breaking this down:<br /> <br /> 1) You're actively teleporting a bullet across the world. This immediately poses three issues:<br /> <br /> 1a) First: inertia. Does the bullet continue as fired, or does it lose it's initial inertia and gain a relative stable inertia to it's new location. If it keeps it's initial inertia, then you now have to magically account for altering that inertia so the bullet goes where you want it to go, instead of whatever direction it was headed before just in a different place. Remember PBD applies as well. If it loses inertia (which is in my mind far more how simple teleportation is indicated as working), then the bullet teleports across the world and without more magic becomes still. This might seem like a dick move for the sniper, but it's very nice for all those Corr 2 coin tricks. If you left your wallet on a train, you don't want to teleport it back to your pocket at 60 mph. And I don't know about you, but I'd rather force the sniper to need more Spheres too pull off shooting a target on the other side of the world, than a mage grabbing their wallet needing to have Forces to avoid it blowing a hole in their clothing.<br /> <br /> 1b) Correspondence 2/Matter 2 can only teleport small things you can physically touch, so... you have to shoot yourself to teleport a bullet with just that. Correspondence 3/Matter 2 would be a minimum to teleport the bullet without touching it. However you're snatching a moving bullet here, which means you need to be using magic to lock on to the bullet (not that this is hard for a Corr 3 character, but it's adding complexity as you're juggling even more effects at once or necessitating even more successes to one big effect). And Correspondence 3 alone could have just let you open a hole in space to shoot through.<br /> <br /> 1c) You have to aim at the target. If you're using a second effect to spot them with your remote viewing goggles, you need to add in Life, otherwise your remote viewing is stuck in one place and can't follow the target around while you're busy teleporting the bullet. Without locking the spell onto a pattern, Correspondence Sensing goes to locations and has to be recast every time you want to change locations (or at Corr 3 you can always view multiple locations, but you still have to recast to change what they are). Remember there's a difficulty penalty if you have lots of effects running at once too. So we're also now into adding Mind 1 to handle aiming the gun where you are, aiming the gun where the target is, and doing that while you're not actually operating the rifle and instead looking through remote view goggles.<br /> <br /> 2) You seem to have very little knowledge of how guns are to be around, and are projecting that as average. <br /> <br /> 2a) Just because you can't see a bullet flying through the air, doesn't mean you can't perceive it (especially the wakes it leaves). It doesn't require any specialized knowledge to hear the difference between a blank and a real bullet being fired. We have more senses than sight, and the speed of the bullet doesn't impact that. The speed of the bullet is mostly something that leaves us unable to react fast enough for it too matter to what the shooter is doing. But the sound of a bullet whizzing through the air and then suddenly not any more is something your average human can hear with ease. Bullets are loud (not just the initial gun shot), especially hypersonic sniper rounds that are causing a constant sonic boom in their wake.<br /> <br /> 2b) It doesn't require above average anything to see where a bullet hits (especially one fired from a high powered sniper rifle) even if it isn't where the shooter seemed to be aiming. It takes even less to hear it even if you don't see where it happened. Bullets don't just disappear even if finding them is frequently more trouble than it's worth (since it's worth very little in most circumstances for the people present to do so). The average person knows a gun being fired means a bullet should hit something, and when that doesn't happen, something weird just happened (aka vulgar).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>That's not how things work, and to prove it I summon the most basic HAP example: <i>A coin appearing from nowhere in your pocket </i></b>(Corr 2 can do that): It's Coincident in HAP, the Observer it's not in your pocket. <b>End of story</b>, or it should be, as that was the example used to distinguish HAP from HOP, if my memory doesn't fail. </div> </div> </div>First, please, the &quot;Coincident&quot; thing is getting a bit confusing. It's Coincidental. They mean different (if related and sometimes overlapping) things, and the distinction is kind of important here.<br /> <br /> Second, no, this isn't the end of the story. This, for instance, is completely vulgar if your pocket was just searched. The HAP is not in your pocket, but the determination is still contextual. It also doesn't work if you summon something too big for your pocket (as directly noted in M20, you can't pull a huge hand gun out of a tiny pocket Coincidentally even if you could pull a coin out of that pocket). It still has to be believable, and a bullet poofing out of existence and going somewhere else isn't something people believe in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Observer Its Hypothetical because it's not a real witness and it's &quot;everywhere&quot;,... </div> </div> </div>Something you're ignoring repeatedly is that second part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The method its intended to determine if a thing it's Vulgar Without Witnesses. </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't. It's intended to determine if a thing is Coincidental or Vulgar. The determination of Vulgar with or without witnesses is made separately.<br /> <br /> As well, the way you're applying things seems determined to eliminate Vulgar w/o witnesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but at the same time the observer isn't a balistic expert that knows how guns work, and where a bullet should land, nor has superhuman senses to follow a bullet, see that it warps outside reality, and then reapears in the other side of the planet. </div> </div> </div>I know a few dozen seven year old kids with the working knowledge of firearms and ballistics to notice the teleportation of a bullet post-firing to somewhere else as weird. Hundreds of millions, if not billions of human beings grow up around guns enough to know this. It's not hard, you don't need to be an expert. You need to have spent a few hours at a range just hearing things, or gone on a few hunting trips.<br /> <br /> As well, you can't both state that the HAP is &quot;everywhere&quot; and insist that something is Coincidental because the HAP is apparently only sitting right behind the shooter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bullets do not suddenly turn mid air that way. </div> </div> </div>Actually, they do, at least if you're being subtle and only adjusting it a degree or two so it barely misses you. Bullets don't turn 90 degrees, but that's overtly vulgar too. Again, your lack of practical knowledge on guns is kinda showing, and projecting it as average is getting frustrating. Wind affects ballistic paths, as does heat, the earth's rotation, and gravity. The perfect ballistic arc only happens in physics class.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HAP does accept a level of goofyness that leaves things without explanation. </div> </div> </div>No, the game bends HAP around a bit to encourage being creative with magic instead of trying to rules lawyer everything. The &quot;coin trick&quot; really shouldn't be Coincidental by HAP if you're teleporting an existing object because the HAP should see the coin being pulled away from where ever you go it from (the logic of it is directly countered when dealing with things like using Correspondence from your Sanctum, since the game insists on both sides of the effect mattering then to avoid Sanctums being Correspondence kiting fests), but it is because it's a game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't make a tiger appear in the zoo because a tiger it's big, and the observer should see it appearing from nowhere (barring obfuscations that would make the spell Vulgar Without Witnesses, like doing it in a closed space that's big enough to harbor a person),... </div> </div> </div>If you acknowledge that even with obfuscation the tiger is still Vulgar w/o Witnesses, then I don't see what the argument is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..and so it's a bullet appearing and blasting something, as bullets do when you're being sniped without your knowledge (if it &quot;lodges&quot; itself in your head without breaking your skull, then yeah, it's Vulgar with or without witnesses). </div> </div> </div>The target isn't the HAP, the HAP is aware of what's going on because you can't obfuscate things from them, remember? As well, I have no idea why you think the bullet lodging in your skull (something that happens all the time with head shots) matters at all to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I seem to remember that HAP critics used your very arguments to favor HOP. </div> </div> </div>I don't care. How someone else used an argument or a similar argument doesn't change if my argument is any good. I mean, I'm pretty sure I saw someone using your arguments to favor burning RPGs for being the tools of the devil . Are you burning RPG books in bouts of religious fanaticism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T10:24:16-07:00","id":1134865,"title":"","content":"I really feel Heavy has said pretty much all that needs to be said. But the rules I'm applying are the ones that Brucato seems to be using (with something less than rigorous application) when he's discussing the relevant issues in M20 (and in Book of Secrets and, even, amidst some of the insanity in HDYDT), irrespective, in some parts of its essence, of trying to mangle discussions of causality with the often ill-defined HAP vs. HOP vs. etc. As witnessed by the fact that your &quot;iron-clad&quot; examples of HAP, keep moving that Observer around to wherever it's most convenient to make your arguments fall out the way you want them too and away from the locations where it makes your argument weaker or even foolish.<br /> <br /> But, putting aside the philosophical issues aside for the practical, if a player with Weapons as an Instrument was trying to shoot someone in head, the necessary Spheres for the Effect would be vary dependent on what's the exact situation and what options were available. This is very different situation if the mage also has Math as an Instrument and is using Entropy and Correspondence to shoot someone within what is considered the range of the weapon vs. another mage who wants to have a bullet appear out of nowhere and smash into someone's head on the opposite side of the world. And the variety of situations makes it difficult to answer the initial question with any degree of specificity.<br /> <br /> Except for needing Matter. Since there's no transformation of substance involved, nor is there anything set up in the question stating that locking an effect into the bullet (or maybe the rifle), there doesn't need to be any Matter. (Unless that's what the character is trying to do.... implant a moving bullet created out of nothing into someone's head from beyond any conceivable range for the rifle in question, but, man, that's about the hardest way possible to do this - a Correspondence3/Life 3/Matter 2/Prime 2 effect. But, it could be Coincidental...)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T12:49:07-07:00","id":1134904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As witnessed by the fact that your &quot;iron-clad&quot; examples of HAP, keep moving that Observer around to wherever it's most convenient to make your arguments fall out the way you want them too and away from the locations where it makes your argument weaker or even foolish.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Observer it's wherever a normal person would be. That's why it isn't in your pocket when you materialize the coin, it isn't touching your pocket, it isn't looking inside your pocket. All of these would make the most basic example of HAB to be Vulgar. You can materialize a gun inside your pockets if it would fit, so you can do with a bullet. All of this it's pure HAB (the example was coined to explain what HAB is long ago, and it's still Coincidental in M20).<br /> <br /> The Observer it's watching where you shoot, so it's watching where the bullet impacts, the observer isn't where the bullet get's lost/dissapears, for the same reason it isn't touching your pocket nor looking inside of it...that would be as much bad faith as making the gun invisible and inaudible to make it &quot;Coincidental&quot;, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> It's a shoot that you loose from sight (and other senses) as it travels as fast as the best rifle can make it/hit someone without anybody knowing where it's the shooter so convoluted and unreal as to shout &quot;IMPOSSIBLE, this cannot be happening!&quot;?<br /> <br /> I think you two are focusing far too much on the &quot;space-warp&quot;, but that isn't the effect the effect it's a relocation of the bullet. I remember a HAP thread where it was argued that a person could teleport coincidentally if in the middle of a crowd (and close distances), because when you're in a crowd it's hard to know how fast you traveled. Nobody started complaining about space warps, dimension doors, and HAP controling where you are and seeing you disappear (in fact, it was argued that only HOO would know your exact position at all times). I think that what I'm talking about it's much less convoluted than that.<br /> <br /> I also don't see how this &quot;destroys&quot; Vulgar Without Witnesses. Obviously opeing a portal to shoot where nobody it's watching (from both sides) would be just that. How it's that saying that, under special circumstances, effects like teleportation could be Coincidental...&quot;destroys VWW&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-28-2017, 04:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T13:30:10-07:00","id":1134921,"title":"","content":"Here, let's have a relevant thread, <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1015604-teleportation-and-coincidence\">Teleportation and Coincidence</a>,</span> to ilustrate different interpretations of where the HAP/HAB/HAO/whatever it's &quot;located&quot;. It seems that Brucato has an even more permisive understanding of HAP than I have...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-28-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T14:54:38-07:00","id":1134960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1134904#post1134904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Observer it's wherever a normal person would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're where they need to be to help judge the vulgarity of the effect. No normal person would share a bathroom stall with me, but that doesn't make bathroom stalls universal Sanctums where you can cast vulgar magic coincidentally because the HAP is too prudish to look at you on the toilet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of these would make the most basic example of HAB to be Vulgar. </div> </div> </div>The most basic example of HAP is not &quot;this is always coincidental&quot; anyway. It is explicitly stated to be contextually on the line, and can move to the vulgar side of the line very easily.<br /> <br /> M20 <b>does not say</b> that teleporting a coin into your pocket is always coincidental because the HAP isn't in your pocket. It says that teleporting a coin into your pocket is <u>usually</u> coincidental because the HAP isn't in your pocket unless the context of the situation says it should be. If my mage holds their pocket open, and coins just appear in the pocket and fall you, the HAP sees that, they aren't blinded to it just because of the &quot;not in your pocket&quot; concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Observer it's watching where you shoot, so it's watching where the bullet impacts, the observer isn't where the bullet get's lost/dissapears, for the same reason it isn't touching your pocket nor looking inside of it...that would be as much bad faith as making the gun invisible and inaudible to make it &quot;Coincidental&quot;, wouldn't it? </div> </div> </div>No. The HAP doesn't notice reasonable things ending up in your pockets because people have stuff in their pockets. I have a coin in my pocket right now. Nobody is going to be surprised when another person pulls a coin out of their pocket unless given a reason to be surprised by it first (as well noted, including in M20). The HAP notices where the bullet disappears because bullets <b>don't disappear</b>. Nobody believes that bullets vanish into thin air the way they believe coins are a natural thing to be in a pocket.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a shoot that you loose from sight (and other senses) as it travels as fast as the best rifle can make it/hit someone without anybody knowing where it's the shooter so convoluted and unreal as to shout &quot;IMPOSSIBLE, this cannot be happening!&quot;? </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter, in the slightest, to a case where teleportation or gates are necessary to hit the target, that snipers can make amazing shots that the people next to the targets are unable to even have a clue of where the bullet came from.<br /> <br /> The hidden sniper isn't even magic, it's just skill. The hitting a target that you couldn't hit in reality that's magic and is the crux of what to examine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you two are focusing far too much on the &quot;space-warp&quot;, but that isn't the effect the effect it's a relocation of the bullet. </div> </div> </div>I think this is an incredibly disingenuous dodge of what we've been saying. I addressed the relocation of the bullet in exhaustive detail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I remember a HAP thread where it was argued that a person could teleport coincidentally if in the middle of a crowd (and close distances), because when you're in a crowd it's hard to know how fast you traveled. </div> </div> </div>I was in that thread! I still do not buy the argument that crowds make teleportation coincidental because the HAP can't see people in crowds, and I don't think anyone successfully made the case for it. There being a thread about it doesn't mean you're preferred interpretation is either correct or the best to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nobody started complaining about space warps, dimension doors, and HAP controling where you are and seeing you disappear (in fact, it was argued that only HOO would know your exact position at all times). I think that what I'm talking about it's much less convoluted than that. </div> </div> </div>Um, you might want to reread the thread you did link to already, since people did start &quot;complaining&quot; about all sorts of crazy stuff from the logic people in the &quot;crowds are mobile teleportation specific Sanctums&quot; side of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also don't see how this &quot;destroys&quot; Vulgar Without Witnesses. </div> </div> </div>Because if you honestly follow the logic in question, there is no situation where Vulgar w/o Witnesses happens due to the HAP always 'missing' the effect and making it coincidental. You're just drawing an arbitrary and inconsistent line of where it happens to deny this logical issue.<br /> <br /> If I can coincidentally shoot someone in New York from Hong Kong by literally teleporting the bullet across space, I can turn into a dragon in a bathroom stall. The HAP is a paper tiger that is always capable of being fooled by a nanosecond's worth of preparations, and the HAP only matters when mages are purposefully trying to do vulgar magic; making it pointless.<br /> <br /> When you acknowledge that creating a tiger out of nothing, even in a box a normal person can't see into, is vulgar, but teleporting objects across the globe is coincidental, you're just setting an arbitrary line, not a logical one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How it's that saying that, under special circumstances, effects like teleportation could be Coincidental...&quot;destroys VWW&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Because you're not just saying, &quot;under special circumstances,&quot; you're arguing that snipers are teleportation magic.<br /> <br /> Under special circumstances for coincidental teleportation are things like a short hop out of a first story room with a window, not out of a hermetically sealed room across the globe because you're wearing a Batman costume and drop a smoke bomb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1134921#post1134921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems that Brucato has an even more permisive understanding of HAP than I have...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, he really doesn't. It helps if you read the whole section not just the Batman reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T18:55:26-07:00","id":1135017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they're where they need to be to help judge the vulgarity of the effect. No normal person would share a bathroom stall with me, but that doesn't make bathroom stalls universal Sanctums where you can cast vulgar magic coincidentally because the HAP is too prudish to look at you on the toilet.<br /> <br /> The most basic example of HAP is not &quot;this is always coincidental&quot; anyway. It is explicitly stated to be contextually on the line, and can move to the vulgar side of the line very easily.<br /> <br /> M20 <b>does not say</b> that teleporting a coin into your pocket is always coincidental because the HAP isn't in your pocket. It says that teleporting a coin into your pocket is <u>usually</u> coincidental because the HAP isn't in your pocket unless the context of the situation says it should be. If my mage holds their pocket open, and coins just appear in the pocket and fall you, the HAP sees that, they aren't blinded to it just because of the &quot;not in your pocket&quot; concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing against that. On the contrary, that example it's the most basic HAP example not because it's always Coincidental, but rather because it shows the limit between HAP and HOP. In HOP, it would never pass as a coincidence, in HAP it can pass. If that example can't possibly be Coincidental, then we aren't in HAP anymore. Other examples that could be Coincidetal under both HAP and HOP wouldn't work so well<br /> <br /> My point it's not, and never was, that the remote sniper effect HAS to be Coincidental. It's stupidly easy to think about how the effect could be Vulgar. You showed very well how to make the rote Vulgar with your portal thing. I myself posted an exaple that, In my opinion, would be Vulgar.<br /> <br /> My point was to find an instance, a way to do it, where the rote could be Coincident. You aren't helping, and thus I must assume you think this can't ever happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. The HAP doesn't notice reasonable things ending up in your pockets because people have stuff in their pockets. I have a coin in my pocket right now. Nobody is going to be surprised when another person pulls a coin out of their pocket unless given a reason to be surprised by it first (as well noted, including in M20). The HAP notices where the bullet disappears because bullets <b>don't disappear</b>. Nobody believes that bullets vanish into thin air the way they believe coins are a natural thing to be in a pocket.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter, in the slightest, to a case where teleportation or gates are necessary to hit the target, that snipers can make amazing shots that the people next to the targets are unable to even have a clue of where the bullet came from.<br /> <br /> The hidden sniper isn't even magic, it's just skill. The hitting a target that you couldn't hit in reality that's magic and is the crux of what to examine. </div> </div> </div>As you yourself say you can &quot;prove&quot; the coin in the pocket it's Vulgar by placing the observer looking inside the pocket. You can &quot;prove&quot; that the Batman example it's vulgar by saying that it was just below the window and touched the mage just before it vanished.<br /> <br /> And that's damaging for this conversation because it's not proving that the spell should be vulgar, but rather that there are special circumstances where it should be vulgar.<br /> <br /> So, let's avoid that.<br /> <br /> Having said that:<br /> <br /> You don't detect anything surprising about people pulling a coin out of their pockets. I'm I right to assume that you think pulling out a bullet would be just as Coincidental?. And if you can materialize the item there, so you can make it vanish as long nobody saw you pulling it there. Nothing weird in not having a bullet in your pocket...Also, you think somebody being shot &quot;out of nowhere&quot; (snipers can make shots that the people next to the targets are unable to even have a clue of where the bullet came from) wouldn't be so surprising either.<br /> <br /> <i>Thus, the problem it's the point where the bullet disappears/reappears, and no other point.</i> That's what you're saying. Am I right?<br /> <br /> <i>Well, then let me rephrase my previous question: </i>If someone Observes a bullet (hearing it too) and then that person stops seeing and hearing it, It would uncanny for the average person to think &quot;oh, that bullet was so fast that it went off my sensory range in an instant&quot;?.<br /> <br /> I get from your answers that bullets just aren't so fast that an average someone might think that the bullet seemed to disappear because it left sensory range (like the Batman dissapears into the night). That just doesn't happen no matter what weapon or ammunition you use.<br /> <br /> If that's the case, would be impossible to produce or take advantage of a circumstance where the Observer MAY be able to, as you say, find the loss of the bullet...unsurprissing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-28-2017, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T21:53:55-07:00","id":1135061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135017#post1135017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing against that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly seems like it is when it comes to the sniper rifle. You're not trying to come up with circumstances that make it coincidental, you're just declaring that the HAP wouldn't notice normal things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point was to find an instance, a way to do it, where the rote could be Coincident. You aren't helping, and thus I must assume you think this can't ever happen. </div> </div> </div>It can't ever happen if it involves shooting someone so far away you have to use Correspondence to teleport the bullet. If you are firing at a target that's within the range of the weapon (something quite considerable for high powered sniper rifles), that's a different matter entirely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's damaging for this conversation because it's not proving that the spell should be vulgar, but rather that there are special circumstances where it should be vulgar. </div> </div> </div>I posted an extremely detailed explanation of why it should be vulgar, and you ignored it. Don't accuse me of &quot;damaging&quot; the discussion for not making my case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, you think somebody being shot &quot;out of nowhere&quot; (snipers can make shots that the people next to the targets are unable to even have a clue of where the bullet came from) wouldn't be so surprising either. </div> </div> </div>So... you want to resurrect this same semantic game from the other teleportation thread? Where the phrasing, &quot;vanish into a crowd,&quot; is somehow literally the ability to vanish from sight for mages?<br /> <br /> Because I pointed out the flaws with this there already.<br /> <br /> When someone is shot, &quot;out of nowhere,&quot; that isn't a literal belief that the sniper can be anywhere on Earth. That's a belief that spotting the sniper is going to be incredibly difficult if not impossible, even if the sniper is somewhere within the range of the weapon.<br /> <br /> People do not belief that bullets can literally appear out of nowhere and strike a target. You're taking a colloquialism and trying to make it a literal belief in direct defiance of how humans think.<br /> <br /> As said in the other thread: the saying that &quot;it's raining cats and dogs,&quot; doesn't make it coincidental to turn heavy rain into cats and dogs. The meaning of the saying matters, not the literal definitions of the words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Thus, the problem it's the point where the bullet disappears/reappears, and no other point.</i> That's what you're saying. Am I right? </div> </div> </div>Not precisely. The problem lies in the bullet having to be teleported at all. &quot;Where&quot; it occurs is largely meaningless in the grand scheme of the debate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Well, then let me rephrase my previous question: </i>If someone Observes a bullet (hearing it too) and then that person stops seeing and hearing it, It would uncanny for the average person to think &quot;oh, that bullet was so fast that it went off my sensory range in an instant&quot;? </div> </div> </div>Yes. Bullets get slower, not faster. If you're sensing a bullet in passing and the sensory inputs only make sense that the bullet suddenly got faster (left your sensory range more rapidly than it should have) it would sound very screwed up to the exceedingly large number of people (enough to call average) that have heard guns being shot..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [If that's the case, would be impossible to produce or take advantage of a circumstance where the Observer MAY be able to, as you say, find the loss of the bullet...unsurprissing? </div> </div> </div>The &quot;loss&quot; of the bullet doesn't justify it traveling 500 miles.<br /> <br /> If I'm standing on the cliffs of Dover and I toss a rock into the English Channel, I don't think there's any reasonable expectation of anyone finding that rock. That doesn't mean there's a reasonable expectation of that rock ending up breaking a window in the White House. The two don't connect. &quot;I can't see where the bullet landed,&quot; doesn't connect to, &quot;The bullet could literally be anywhere on the planet.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T02:27:39-07:00","id":1135105,"title":"","content":"I think, Heavy Arms, Aleph's simple point is:<br /> <br /> 1) HAB #1 at the sniper's location: Sees the sniper shoot. Sure, he might simply shoot off into the distance, nonsensically, but nothing happens that makes a HAB go 'This is impossible!'<br /> 2) HAB #2 at the target's location: Sees the target being shot from somewhere. Nothing happens that makes the HAB go 'This is impossible!' as they look around and do not spot the 'hidden sniper' that could realistically be, well, hidden somewhere.<br /> <br /> This is under the presumption that the target *is* in a location that would allow a far away theoretical (but in this case nonexistant) sniper to shoot them. if the target would be, say, in a closed room, things go paradox instantly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Only if we assume a HAB that can see *both* places at *once* that we run into constant Vulgar/Paradox issues no matter the placement - but at *that* point we are crossing into dreaded HOO territory.<br /> A HOO can see the bullet travelling much further than it should/could. A HOO can see everywhere, everything.<br /> <br /> A HAB can't do that. And a HAB could never see both places at once either. They have the theoretical senses and placement of a normal person.<br /> Your example of somebody &quot;vanishing inside the crowd&quot; being paradox fits HAB induced paradox perfectly - a hypothetical person walking next to the Mage in the crowd would see them vanish.<br /> It's hard to go paradox with a HAB with the sniper rote, as no matter where you place the HAB, things would not look impossible - for better or for worse.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> To add, in the end a ST might simply rule it Vulgar for balancing reasons, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-29-2017, 05:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T06:55:53-07:00","id":1135146,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:13px\">Indeed, that was my point, and Heavy was saying that such thing it's impossible because the average person would totally sense it. And with the &quot;vanishing in a crowd&quot; example, I stated that I thought my example was much less convluted, not that the &quot;vanishing in a crowd&quot; wasn't convoluted. I wouldn't allow that for the reasons you stated. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It can't ever happen if it involves shooting someone so far away you have to use Correspondence to teleport the bullet. If you are firing at a target that's within the range of the weapon (something quite considerable for high powered sniper rifles), that's a different matter entirely.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">You can use Forces to increase the range of the weapon beyond anything conventional snipers can do (trough not as much as in my example, by a long shot) merely by decreasing friction and increasing the force of the bullet. It's that different example Vulgar too, in your opinion, as it's no longer &quot;the range of the weapon&quot;?. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">When someone is shot, &quot;out of nowhere,&quot; that isn't a literal belief that the sniper can be anywhere on Earth. </span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When someone pulls a coin from his pocket there isn't a literal belief that the person can be pulling the coin from thin air, nor that pockets somehow &quot;create matter&quot;.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's a belief that spotting the sniper is going to be incredibly difficult if not impossible, even if the sniper is somewhere within the range of the weapon.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">When someone pulls a coin from it's pocket there's the belief the coin was there all the time, not that it was produced from Quintessence.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Why would the sniper have to be close if the coin doesn't have to be close? Why would the sniper have to *exist*, if the coin doesn't? . </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">People do not belief that bullets can literally appear out of nowhere and strike a target.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Same with coins. They can't appear from nowhere, but they can appear from nowhere if they do so inside a pocket and no one it's looking. This is because people believes that pockets contain stuff, as you yourself said, not because they believe stuff appears out of nowhere inside pockets. Bullets do not appear out of nowhere, but that's not enough to call the apparition Vulgar under HAP.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">You're taking a colloquialism and trying to make it a literal belief in direct defiance of how humans think.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No, I'm assuming that humans won't think that the bullet come literally &quot;out of nowhere&quot;, just as I'm assuming humans won't think that the coin was materialized inside the pocket but rather was there all along.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Not precisely. The problem lies in the bullet having to be teleported at all. &quot;Where&quot; it occurs is largely meaningless in the grand scheme of the debate.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Why where a coin appears it's important (it has to be a pocket or an appropiate container) but where a bullet appears isn't important? I could make a coin disappear from a pocket in the other side of the planet and reapear in my pocket, any HAP defender would say it's Coincidental unless I robbed someone that was very aware of how much change she had. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Of course it's important *where* things teleport, you can argue that there isn't a place in planet Earth where this would be Coincidental, even under HAP, but not that &quot;</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">the bullet having to be teleported at all</span><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot; it's the problem. In fact, there is a simple Coincidental rote: making your weapon shoot a bullet more than it's total capacity, which implies creating or teleporting a bullet inside the chamber.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">The &quot;loss&quot; of the bullet doesn't justify it traveling 500 miles.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It doesn't have to, under HAP. You're muddling the discussion by pointing out all these examples that are more appropiate for HOP than for HAP (and I'm not discussing HAP vs HOP). All that you needed to clarify to me to mantain that the rote it's Vulgar was the following:</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Bullets get slower, not faster. If you're sensing a bullet in passing and the sensory inputs only make sense that the bullet suddenly got faster (left your sensory range more rapidly than it should have) it would sound very screwed up to the exceedingly large number of people (enough to call average) that have heard guns being shot..</span> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since I don't know much about firearms, I asked if an average observer couldn't easily rationalize the teleportation as the shoot being fast enough to leave sensory range. If you think it's impossible to rationalize that the bullet dissapeared by going out of range, well I have no authority to say otherwise. That's, literally, all that I needed to read.</span></b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-29-2017, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T08:10:01-07:00","id":1135160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1134862#post1134862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a few dozen seven year old kids with the working knowledge of firearms and ballistics to notice the teleportation of a bullet post-firing to somewhere else as weird. Hundreds of millions, if not billions of human beings grow up around guns enough to know this. It's not hard, you don't need to be an expert. You need to have spent a few hours at a range just hearing things, or gone on a few hunting trips.</div> </div> </div> </div> I really have to disagree with this. I think you are highly overstating average gun knowledge, let alone knowledge of how bullets sound versus a bullet vanishing mid-air, let alone it being from a sniper rifle.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T10:58:30-07:00","id":1135204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135105#post1135105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I1) HAB #1 at the sniper's location: Sees the sniper shoot. Sure, he might simply shoot off into the distance, nonsensically, but nothing happens that makes a HAB go 'This is impossible!'</div> </div> </div> </div>The bullet literally vanishing into thin air makes the HAB go &quot;This is impossible&quot; or a #3 HAB does so if this happens far enough away from the shooter that you need a second one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only if we assume a HAB that can see *both* places at *once* that we run into constant Vulgar/Paradox issues no matter the placement - but at *that* point we are crossing into dreaded HOO territory. </div> </div> </div>Nope. See above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have the theoretical senses and placement of a normal person. </div> </div> </div>The &quot;normal person&quot; placement is being taken to an absurd place. I can't fire a bullet and it magically transforms into a dog, and it will be coincidental because the HAP is looking at me, the shooter, and not looking at where the bullet's path is at all.<br /> <br /> If you agree that transmuting the bullet into a dog after it's passed out of the sensory ranges of the HAP by me, why is it OK to ignore the HAP dealing watching the path of the bullet in the sniper case?<br /> <br /> Because that's the crux of the issue to me in all this. It relies on the placement of the HAP being not where it could see the magic happening, and only where the mage and the target are.<br /> <br /> Oddly, you and Alpeh are making the <b>exact</b> argument people were using to say it's coincidental for a mage to &quot;vanish into a crowd&quot; to make Forces 2 invisibility coincidental. They argued extensively about how the HAP wouldn't see that, because once you vanish into the crowd, the HAP doesn't see you do it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's hard to go paradox with a HAB with the sniper rote, as no matter where you place the HAB, things would not look impossible - for better or for worse. </div> </div> </div>Please cite for me any time a sniper has fired a rifle and killed someone 500 miles away.<br /> <br /> Beyond all this HOP/HAP stuff (also, that whole vanishing into the crowd thread did result in the exact same &quot;HOP&quot; name calling you and Aleph are resorting to here where disagreeing with someone's claim that HAP doesn't see something, that the other person doesn't understand HAP and is just a HOP enthusiast), the point of all of this terminology is to try to draw game-play lines for when magic is <b>Coincidental</b> in the sense that it is believable in the Reality Zone you're in as occurring without magic. How does a bullet travel 500 miles instantly through space in the current Consensus Reality Zone of the game?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135146#post1135146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can use Forces to increase the range of the weapon beyond anything conventional snipers can do (trough not as much as in my example, by a long shot) merely by decreasing friction and increasing the force of the bullet. It's that different example Vulgar too, in your opinion, as it's no longer &quot;the range of the weapon&quot;?.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's more situational? Also the M20 rules basically self limit this by having the bullet get destroyed as you accelerate it past it's structural tolerances by accelerating it that fast (which is not just air resistance, and this gets complicated enough to do that the bullet basically becomes a Wonder - if a weak and cheap one - and we're supposed to be more relaxed with vulgarity with such things). Range also isn't some set precise figure regardless of what the gun's stats are listed as (either in the books or in the real world). How far a bullet can travel is impacted by a large number of variables (I mean, you've already looked at the difference between what's considered the effective range of a weapon versus what the theoretical range estimates are and they're pretty big differences)<br /> <br /> Unless you completely reduce drag (again, not just friction) the impact of drag scales up with initial velocity, and unless you completely eliminate gravity, the bullet will fall back to the ground no matter how fast it's going.<br /> <br /> So sure, you want to pull off a 3 mile shot? Coincidental all day, it's possible, if highly improbably, and you're just using magic to make it doable. 6 miles? Probably. Significantly past the theoretical maximums of a sniper rifle? The bullet destroys itself from the excess force as per the rules on such anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why would the sniper have to be close if the coin doesn't have to be close? Why would the sniper have to *exist*, if the coin doesn't? </div> </div> </div>1) Well, the coin being close does actually matter... the HAP example doesn't mean you don't have to deal with the Correspondence range issues.<br /> <br /> 2) And the important thing here is that the coin is hidden from the HAP until revealed. A bullet flying through the air isn't. You can't shoot someone in a fashion that's completely obscured.<br /> <br /> If you want to magically kill someone and create the injury and evidence of a bullet wound... that's a very different thing than actually sniping someone with Correspondence from a different city. Which would be an actual comparison to the coin trick in concept even if not in Sphere's used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, I'm assuming that humans won't think that the bullet come literally &quot;out of nowhere&quot;, just as I'm assuming humans won't think that the coin was materialized inside the pocket but rather was there all along. </div> </div> </div>Which is... why I'm very focused on the shooter side of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course it's important *where* things teleport, </div> </div> </div>I meant where as in the location of the bullet as it is being teleported relevant to the shooter (aka at the barrel of the gun, or a 100m away) doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> [quote]It doesn't have to, under HAP.['quote]<br /> <br /> Yes, it does. You're getting so focused on HAP, that you're ignoring the entire point of &quot;Coincidental&quot; in the first place. The spell needs to be something that humans can pass off as coincidence. The books make it clear that Correspondence is not supposed to be a free pass on this (that is, you can't use the separation of space to hide the vulgar stuff from one side of the effect). There is no coincidence in a bullet traveling 500 miles and shooting someone in the head. That doesn't happen. Nobody witnesses that and goes, &quot;well, that's believable.&quot; and adding teleportation to &quot;hide&quot; it from people watching is not how HAP is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> Or let me put it this way:<br /> <br /> Explain why teleportation sniping is Coincidental, but I can't use Correspondence to transmute a bullet into a dog mid teleportation to have a dog appear out of nowhere in an alley next to someone for whatever reason I have to do so (dogs live in alleys!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're muddling the discussion by pointing out all these examples that are more appropiate for HOP than for HAP (and I'm not discussing HAP vs HOP) </div> </div> </div>No, you're treating HOP as a magical incantation to win Internet debates.<br /> <br /> Just to be abundantly clear: Every time you've mentioned HOP, the only thing you've communicated to me is that you don't have an actual counter point, so you need to paint me as a killjoy HOP fanatic to dismiss what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All that you needed to clarify to me to mantain that the rote it's Vulgar was the following: </div> </div> </div>Don't blame me if you didn't ask the question you wanted more clearly, and I did answer this previously anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135160#post1135160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really have to disagree with this. I think you are highly overstating average gun knowledge, let alone knowledge of how bullets sound versus a bullet vanishing mid-air, let alone it being from a sniper rifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, since teleportation is impossible, I don't have a direct real world thing to compare it to.<br /> <br /> I do however, know plenty of kids here that are from hunting families (which is extremely common, especially when you account for all of people, even in the US, 2/3s of people have had some firearms experience, even if most of them are not avid shooters). I've seen them all recognize the difference between a .22 (extremely common hunting around) and a 30-08 (extremely common big game round and close to many smaller sniper rifles), and a full cartridge and a blank. It doesn't take much, because they actually sound different.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T11:29:35-07:00","id":1135219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135204#post1135204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do however, know plenty of kids here that are from hunting families (which is extremely common, especially when you account for all of people, even in the US, 2/3s of people have had some firearms experience, even if most of them are not avid shooters). I've seen them all recognize the difference between a .22 (extremely common hunting around) and a 30-08 (extremely common big game round and close to many smaller sniper rifles), and a full cartridge and a blank. It doesn't take much, because they actually sound different.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And I know plenty of people not from hunting families with no/limited firearms experience who can't recognize the difference between these things. But these anecdotes aren't very helpful. While most people have <i>some </i>gun experience in the U.S., that's not the same as necessarily being able to recognize the sound of a bullet traveling through air or not, considering experience varies widely. Given that most households don't own guns in the U.S., I'd say though, the day to day knowledge isn't average. As well as the fact the United States is going to be very tilted compared to the rest of the world as far as experience because of the much higher gun ownership rates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 08-29-2017, 02:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T14:27:47-07:00","id":1135268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135204#post1135204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bullet literally vanishing into thin air makes the HAB go &quot;This is impossible&quot; or a #3 HAB does so if this happens far enough away from the shooter that you need a second one.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is the core issue why we two are not agreeing on this - I do not think any person can simply observe a supersonic bullet with their eyes flying mid-air, *and* also see it vanish, *and* then freak out over any impossibilities instead of thinking they just lost track of it.<br /> You are completely ignoring the fact that the bullet is not sitting idly on a table as it goes 'poof'. It does so while in a state that is pretty much impossible for the human eye to keep track of - that is the *key* to this rote: You are making the thing being teleported away impossible to methodically observe in the first place. Through mundane means. *Then* it gets teleported while in that state. *And* it's expected to get into that mundanely unobservable state. It's not the correspondence that is being used to make things coincidental - it's the nature of a tiny, insanely fast moving thing.<br /> It's the essential component, the very trick to it all. Else you'd not have to bother with a rifle in the first place. Just Corr/Force it right off said table and to the target and take paradox either way.<br /> <br /> <br /> The are, yes, certain circumstances where things get paradoxical even with said fired bullet of course. This rote actually needs a lot more than a little prep work to make it worth the while:<br /> <br /> * If the bullet before vanishing was bound to hit X to even the normal observer, but X never did get hit. That's a paradox. So that takes aim into an open field to keep that at bay.<br /> * Second, if the bullet appears in an enclosed room, or from an angle from which there clearly no shooting is possible. Definitely paradox. That means the target *has* to be in an open space that would at the same time make a hidden shooter plausible. Tricky depending on the surroundings.<br /> * Third, If the bullet hits but there is no firing sound *at all*...paradox. I think even the average person these days has at least an idea that silencers are not really movie-silent. Which is, amusingly, a thing we need Forces for again - to bring the sound along. Else people just see a head explode without any sound - paradox as hell.<br /> <br /> All that makes the rote a hassle that needs several preparation steps.<br /> <br /> However, this is the core difference to, as you mention, turning a bullet into a dog: Somebody simply looking down the example alley would see a dog appearing out of thin air, and there is no way to explain that away. A dog is not tiny enough, nor fast enough to be missed appearing in the middle of a street. Now making the dog burst out of a garbage pile, some cardbord boxes or whatever...that's doable. A dog is like a reverse bullet in the way that it needs to appear from inside obstructions or containers, while a bullet must not. Which again shows that the type, size, speed and nature of the object and the things people expect from it are key to this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oddly, you and Alpeh are making the <b>exact</b> argument people were using to say it's coincidental for a mage to &quot;vanish into a crowd&quot; to make Forces 2 invisibility coincidental. </div> </div> </div>As I said..the 'vanish into a crowd' trick most definitely would be paradoxical as hell. Somebody standing next to the vanishing Mage would not be able to 'explain away' the sudden disappearance of a person in front of their eyes in any way. 'Vanish into a crowd' is highly ironic given that some member of the crowd <i>can see you vanish</i>. You don't even need a theoretical observer for that one. There are literal ones in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've seen them all recognize the difference between a .22 (extremely common hunting around) and a 30-08 (extremely common big game round and close to many smaller sniper rifles), and a full cartridge and a blank. It doesn't take much, because they actually sound different. </div> </div> </div>And would they think &quot;Something impossible is happening!&quot; because the sound was different? Would they go 'This is impossible in any way!'? Or would they simply go &quot;Huh? That was weird.&quot;<br /> Seriously, how they would react if a rifle shot suddenly sounded strange? I bet they would instead tell you reasons. What was odd about that one bullet, or casing, or thermal compound, or how the rifling might be messed up. Although I'm not sure on the last part making a difference, really.<br /> <br /> And people finding reasons, instead of not being able to come up with an explanation, is *exactly* what coincidental Magick is about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-29-2017, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T16:15:37-07:00","id":1135289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135219#post1135219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that most households don't own guns in the U.S., I'd say though, the day to day knowledge isn't average. As well as the fact the United States is going to be very tilted compared to the rest of the world as far as experience because of the much higher gun ownership rates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keeping in mind that a significant portion of the non-owner households have people that don't own because they use range guns instead of keeping a gun in their home in the US, there's 1 gun for every 10 people on Earth (and that's all people) just counting <b>civilian owned and registered</b> guns. So that's not counting the number of civilians in a country like Israel that have guns in their homes but the guns are owned by the state, and Israel is also a country with compulsory service (not the only one) where even if private ownership is exceedingly rare, the vast majority of the population has significant firearms training. This is also ignoring all the guns in the hands of criminals, rebel and militia groups in failed states, and countries that just don't track/register gun ownership.<br /> <br /> The whole weird US private gun stockpiling thing is, indeed, something that tilts the stats, but it's not that hard to peel back that outlier and look at guns not really being that rare for most people on Earth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135268#post1135268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is the core issue why we two are not agreeing on this - I do not think any person can simply observe a supersonic bullet with their eyes flying mid-air, *and* also see it vanish, *and* then freak out over any impossibilities instead of thinking they just lost track of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And... why can the HAP only use their eyes again? I've addressed this precise point already. A HAP standing at the right spot is going to hear the crack of the supersonic bullet just end suddenly instead of having the continuous wave of sound that would happen naturally. While it would happen much faster, imagine you're listening to an air horn blast, and it just cuts out completely. It doesn't end with the normal sound waves that you're used to hearing, it doesn't peter out like it was out of air. The sound just goes away like someone muted it. You would notice this. You would notice this even if you weren't familiar with air horns, because you've been hearing your whole life, and we're not used to sounds just cutting out suddenly like that. It would sound completely wrong, because you've got years of experience with sound waves not doing that (because they don't naturally do that).<br /> <br /> Even if you don't want to meet that &quot;That's impossible!&quot; with that, it would still be the, &quot;That makes no sense&quot; threshold on an instinctive level.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are completely ignoring the fact that the bullet is not sitting idly on a table as it goes 'poof'. </div> </div> </div>Actually... that's been a pretty fundamental part of my argument regarding things like sonic boom sound screwing up, or things like the HAP not seeing the bullet actually hit something because the bullet has to actually hit something at some point. The HAP, because of that H, can see the bullet impact even if an actual person wouldn't. It's not some hidden event.<br /> <br /> Again, going back to my Cliffs of Dover example, from the top of the cliffs, you're not going to see or hear the rock splash into the water. That doesn't mean the HAPs wouldn't find it impossible for a rock to hit the water without sound or splash.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are making the thing being teleported away impossible to methodically observe in the first place. </div> </div> </div>Except, of course, you aren't:<br /> <br /> [url]https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rpLAqI1vnZ0[url]<br /> <br /> Or just search for &quot;bullet trace&quot; videos. If you watch these, and you don't need a lick of training or know almost anything about guns, you can see the air distortion of the bullet (it's not always easy, but it's there) from a high powered round. The video above even managed to have a shot highlighted to demonstrate with the right conditions you see the bullet as well.<br /> <br /> It's subtle, but it's completely visible, thus something completely possible to methodically observe in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the bullet before vanishing was bound to hit X to even the normal observer, but X never did get hit. </div> </div> </div>And this is <b>always</b> going to happen with a fired round and a HAP. The HAP isn't distracted by all the other stuff around them, they're in position to see where the bullet should hit, and doesn't. The &quot;open field&quot; is for non-hypothetical witnesses not seeing where the bullet went.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 'Vanish into a crowd' is highly ironic given that some member of the crowd <i>can see you vanish</i>. You don't even need a theoretical observer for that one. There are literal ones in the first place. </div> </div> </div>But they &quot;can&quot; see you, but they don't see you, because you've disappeared into the crowd and the average person doesn't really see the other people in the crowd because they're not actively looking. Just like the average person doesn't see bullet trace, or listen to bullet sonic booms or see impacts in an open field.<br /> <br /> That's the issue here. You're not actually being consistent in application of all this. The vanishing in the crowd thing is BS, because someone actually watching - what the HAP does - would see the impact of the magic. The teleporting bullet would have the same issue. Bullets are not outside the sensory range of average humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or would they simply go &quot;Huh? That was weird.&quot; Seriously, how they would react if a rifle shot suddenly sounded strange? </div> </div> </div>And if you saw someone pull a two foot sword out of a baseball hat (not Coincidental according to the book!), would you say, &quot;That's impossible!&quot; or assume it's a trick and try to explain away the sleight of hand clearly involved? How Sleepers rationalize seeing vulgar magic doesn't make it not-vulgar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And people finding reasons, instead of not being able to come up with an explanation, is *exactly* what coincidental Magick is about. </div> </div> </div>Then there's no vulgar magic at all, because humans rationalize anything they don't understand as a matter of course. We don't believe the impossible is possible, so we invent explanations to explain how it wasn't impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T17:34:19-07:00","id":1135300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the