suddenly like that. It would sound completely wrong, because you've got years of experience with sound waves not doing that (because they don't naturally do that).<br /> <br /> Even if you don't want to meet that &quot;That's impossible!&quot; with that, it would still be the, &quot;That makes no sense&quot; threshold on an instinctive level.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Actually... that's been a pretty fundamental part of my argument regarding things like sonic boom sound screwing up, or things like the HAP not seeing the bullet actually hit something because the bullet has to actually hit something at some point. The HAP, because of that H, can see the bullet impact even if an actual person wouldn't. It's not some hidden event.<br /> <br /> Again, going back to my Cliffs of Dover example, from the top of the cliffs, you're not going to see or hear the rock splash into the water. That doesn't mean the HAPs wouldn't find it impossible for a rock to hit the water without sound or splash.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Except, of course, you aren't:<br /> <br /> [url]https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rpLAqI1vnZ0[url]<br /> <br /> Or just search for &quot;bullet trace&quot; videos. If you watch these, and you don't need a lick of training or know almost anything about guns, you can see the air distortion of the bullet (it's not always easy, but it's there) from a high powered round. The video above even managed to have a shot highlighted to demonstrate with the right conditions you see the bullet as well.<br /> <br /> It's subtle, but it's completely visible, thus something completely possible to methodically observe in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And this is <b>always</b> going to happen with a fired round and a HAP. The HAP isn't distracted by all the other stuff around them, they're in position to see where the bullet should hit, and doesn't. The &quot;open field&quot; is for non-hypothetical witnesses not seeing where the bullet went.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But they &quot;can&quot; see you, but they don't see you, because you've disappeared into the crowd and the average person doesn't really see the other people in the crowd because they're not actively looking. Just like the average person doesn't see bullet trace, or listen to bullet sonic booms or see impacts in an open field.<br /> <br /> That's the issue here. You're not actually being consistent in application of all this. The vanishing in the crowd thing is BS, because someone actually watching - what the HAP does - would see the impact of the magic. The teleporting bullet would have the same issue. Bullets are not outside the sensory range of average humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And if you saw someone pull a two foot sword out of a baseball hat (not Coincidental according to the book!), would you say, &quot;That's impossible!&quot; or assume it's a trick and try to explain away the sleight of hand clearly involved? How Sleepers rationalize seeing vulgar magic doesn't make it not-vulgar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then there's no vulgar magic at all, because humans rationalize anything they don't understand as a matter of course. We don't believe the impossible is possible, so we invent explanations to explain how it wasn't impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, I'm going to have to agree with Aleph. You've gone well beyond &quot;Hypothetical Average Observer&quot; and well into &quot;Hypothetical Omniscient Observer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your argument breaks down into 'if this Hypothetically utterly average person was actually intensely watching every step of what was done, then they would notice a number of extremely subtle differences and then it would be vulgar.'<br /> <br /> This breaks even ESTABLISHED coincidental effects like 'finding' that your cheap beer was 'mislabeled' at the factory and is actually really high quality beer. Because the observer would notice the change in the liquid within.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And to be somewhat clear, this is at least my personal guideline for the difference between 'coincidental' and 'vulgar without witnesses'<br /> <br /> Could you have a sleeper stand nearby and watch you, (The Hypothetical Average Observer) and have them not question you too much about what just happened.<br /> <br /> Materializing a tiger in a bathroom, if there was a witness, would be unexplainable. They would immediately jump to &quot;WTF?!&quot; This doesn't happen, and the absence of a witness doesn't change that in general, if people DID witness it, it would be vulgar.<br /> <br /> People lose track of fast moving, small objects flying through the air all the time. Trust me. I once worked at a golf course.<br /> <br /> Now mind you, again, the audience can have an effect on this. The Technocracy can pull off a lot of nonsense, but if they take some of their gear out in front of a team of sleeper researchers who know their stuff, Those jetboots are going to get mighty vulgar mighty quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 08-29-2017, 09:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-29T18:46:50-07:00","id":1135311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135300#post1135300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You've gone well beyond &quot;Hypothetical Average Observer&quot; and well into &quot;Hypothetical Omniscient Observer.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Please actually demonstrate how any of my arguments have done this... at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your argument breaks down into 'if this Hypothetically utterly average person was actually intensely watching every step of what was done, then they would notice a number of extremely subtle differences and then it would be vulgar.' </div> </div> </div>Because this is <b>a completely false characterization</b> of my statements.<br /> <br /> I've been intensely focused on a very, very, very specific step on why the vulgarity is clearly within the realms of the HAP standard: the bullet disappearing in the open air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This breaks even ESTABLISHED coincidental effects like 'finding' that your cheap beer was 'mislabeled' at the factory and is actually really high quality beer. Because the observer would notice the change in the liquid within. </div> </div> </div>Where is this established?<br /> <br /> Besides that, not really. Beer gets mislabeled (though rarely in major factories since they're not making multiple labels in the same production line for the most part, order a microbrew), unlike bullets disappearing and reappearing 500 miles away to hit a target in the head. Of course the whole &quot;how do you spin this&quot; thing isn't what HAP vs. HOP is about. Either doesn't care about spin. That's why they're hypothetical individuals. They're not there to listen to your character's spin to avoid witnesses or to pull on mythic threads. The see what's going on without all that. The difference is in how much they can see.<br /> <br /> As well, the one beer into a different but extremely similar beer is HAP coincidental because it could be done without any way to see without a chemical analysis. If you're keeping the color of the beer the same... there's nothing you can see, smell, hear, extra from sealed bottle/can of beer. If you're dealing with a clear bottled IPA and you change it into a dark stout... the HAP would notice the vulgar change of color going on.<br /> <br /> The primary core of my argument here is that the bullet, once fired, is observable by the HAP the whole time (I know I fucked up the BBcode, but the video I linked to shows that you can see bullet air displacement), and changes to the state of the bullet (including teleportation) needs to be subtle or the HAP gets set off. Some directional alterations that could be accounted for with environmental factors? Fine. Getting a shot at extreme ranges for the weapon? Fine. There's nothing for the HAP to observe that would be noticeably off. The bullet up and disappearing mid-flight? That's not possible, and it is at least indirectly observable (with bullet trace, sound, and impact site all being things that would alert the HAP that things did not go as they should).<br /> <br /> But at this rate I'm going to have to write a big post that you're all confusing HAP with HYP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 08-29-2017, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:24:48-07:00","id":1135397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135289#post1135289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keeping in mind that a significant portion of the non-owner households have people that don't own because they use range guns instead of keeping a gun in their home in the US, there's 1 gun for every 10 people on Earth (and that's all people) just counting <b>civilian owned and registered</b> guns. So that's not counting the number of civilians in a country like Israel that have guns in their homes but the guns are owned by the state, and Israel is also a country with compulsory service (not the only one) where even if private ownership is exceedingly rare, the vast majority of the population has significant firearms training. This is also ignoring all the guns in the hands of criminals, rebel and militia groups in failed states, and countries that just don't track/register gun ownership.<br /> <br /> The whole weird US private gun stockpiling thing is, indeed, something that tilts the stats, but it's not that hard to peel back that outlier and look at guns not really being that rare for most people on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div> And a significant portion of gun owners don't regularly go to range (only 52% sometimes or often go to the range). And as far as ownership goes, if we're talking people who actually own a gun versus just living in a household that has a gun, the number drops further as far as overall distribution. So in America we have 42% of adults who live in a household with a gun. Around 30% that personally own a gun. Then there is the fact that those who own guns are more likely to own multiple guns, 66% of owners have more than one, if we're talking about distribution.<br /> <br /> If if we really want to talk worldwide, we can look at countries with extremely strict gun laws like England or China in constrast. Guns not being rare on earth isn't close to the claim that the average person can differentiate these vanishing bullet sounds, still even assuming the sound is quite so evident. On a whim I asked my uncle who is a hunter and he didn't feel confident he could identify the difference between a bullet and blank off-hand. Which even brings the idea that just have gun ownership and gun experience necessarily equips one to identify the sounds in question with much accuracy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T05:58:30-07:00","id":1135411,"title":"","content":"Teleport something small in your pocket: coincidental (most times)<br /> Teleport something in an open space: vulgar<br /> <br /> Keep it simple, guys. As long as it's observable by any person around it's vulgar and that's it. No need to drop weapon distribution statistics or anything.<br /> <br /> Another way to look at it (from a ST perspective): Is that rote powerfull enough to break the game? Then it's vulgar. There's always something to make any effect vulgar in specific situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T06:50:08-07:00","id":1135423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135411#post1135411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to look at it (from a ST perspective): Is that rote powerfull enough to break the game? Then it's vulgar. There's always something to make any effect vulgar in specific situations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, hence me saying that STs might turn it vulgar simply for balancing reasons.<br /> *I* would, for that very reason. I simply disagree that it would be under normal HAP rules. But I'd turn it vulgar if I was STing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:00:12-07:00","id":1135468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135397#post1135397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If if we really want to talk worldwide, we can look at countries with extremely strict gun laws like England or China in constrast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is... basically missing the whole point I made about privately own guns (extremely restricted in China) vs. state owned guns. China have ~1.5 million active ground soldiers (that's not their whole military... that's just their people that fight on the ground), and ~1.5 million members of their armed police force (again, distinct from the larger police and state security forces); yes there is (probably China doesn't exactly publish much about this) a good amount of feeding from one into the other, but those are their official numbers for &quot;at a give time.&quot; So despite China's highly restrictive gun laws leading to very low private ownership rates.. there's a lot of people in China that know how to shoot.<br /> <br /> Strict gun laws also don't directly correlate to gun ownership rates (even if they decrease the US's uniquely weird distribution issues); though quantifying the strictness of gun laws is tricky to do an actual correlation with. Lots of EU countries (the EU has strong gun laws as part of membership in general, on top of any local restrictions which are common) have relatively high numbers of civilian guns. Canada and Australia are up there too. There are countries where guns are just outright banned too, but for the most part private gun ownership is more culturally linked than legally linked (though they do play into each other over a long enough period; Japan's gun laws are so strong banning private ownership would barely have an impact but gun bans are so old there's no gun culture like there are in lots of European/Western countries where people will jump through the hoops anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a whim I asked my uncle... </div> </div> </div>Wait, didn't you just say anecdotes aren't helpful, and I responded by not continuing with anecdotes?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135411#post1135411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep it simple, guys. As long as it's observable by any person around it's vulgar and that's it. No need to drop weapon distribution statistics or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that the vast majority of this thread is basically arguing over whether bullets in flight are an observable phenomenon by &quot;average&quot; people, which is why the distribution thing comes up. Even if people stop arguing that bullets aren't observable (I kind of hope after posting a url for a video showing real time visible bullet air distortion this is somewhat put to rest), the argument then moves to can an &quot;average&quot; person see them and recognize that something weird (like the teleportation of the bullet) occurred. Because it if isn't &quot;average&quot; then I'm not applying HAP, but HOP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:13:38-07:00","id":1135474,"title":"","content":"That's what's most important, in my opinion, if bullets in flight (and it's hypotetical vanishment) are an observable phenomenon by &quot;average&quot; people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Teleport something small in your pocket: coincidental (most times)<br /> Teleport something in an open space: vulgar<br /> <br /> Keep it simple, guys. As long as it's observable by any person around it's vulgar and that's it. No need to drop weapon distribution statistics or anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I don't know, the statistics and facts are there to determine if it's observable &quot;by any person arround&quot; or not. There can be debate over if someting it's observable or not. It's important to understand why this is a thing in order to use it where you don't have things like &quot;pockets&quot;, or &quot;open spaces&quot;, but do have comparable situations. But I appreciate your common sense. It's what you need to use &quot;on the fly&quot; when you are playing.<br /> <br /> Pockets work because of two reasons:<br /> *It's imperceptible. Normaly, people can't see what happens in your pocket.<br /> *It plays with people expectations. People takes stuff out of their pockets all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another way to look at it (from a ST perspective): Is that rote powerfull enough to break the game? Then it's vulgar. There's always something to make any effect vulgar in specific situations.<br /> <br /> Yeah, hence me saying that STs might turn it vulgar simply for balancing reasons. </div> </div> </div>Is the rote so powerful, though?. I tought that, with Corr 3, there were better ways to kill people at range. Ways that don't leave bullets, don't attract the police, and may even be much easier to pass as Coincidental (distracting the person with Mind 2-3 so it doesn't see a car when crossing the street, giving Entropy 2-3 bad luck in a moment where luck was <i>really </i>important, infecting the person with a lethal sickness with Life 3. Only the last one may be Vulgar, under HOP, and if you took care of using common dieases in the area and the general health state of the victim, it may even pass that harder test)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Well, the coin being close does actually matter... the HAP example doesn't mean you don't have to deal with the Correspondence range issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>The distance of the teleportation isn't relevant to Vulgarity, as long as both sides of the teleportation are Coicidental (like, say, moving a small talisman between the pocket of the coat you forgot in the airport and the one you're wearing), the object can be moved regardless of how impossible this is (creating items from nothing isn't any more possible than that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just to be abundantly clear: Every time you've mentioned HOP, the only thing you've communicated to me is that you don't have an actual counter point, so you need to paint me as a killjoy HOP fanatic to dismiss what I'm saying. </div> </div> </div>Your examples needed to clarify that the observer should see/hear the bullet when it disappears as something exeedingly strange (as you argumented, latter, in your post), but you obscured them by saying that people do not believe in bullets coming &quot;out of nowhere&quot;, that bullets do not disappear, that the problem it's <i>&quot;the bullet having to be teleported at all&quot;. </i><br /> <br /> It's largely unimportant what people believes about what's <i>really </i>happening, what's important it's what people believes about what they <i>perceive </i>to happen...and that's the whole point. When you read someone's mind, <i>what's really happening </i>it's that you're readinghis mind, and that is impossible, but what people <i>perceives</i> it's...usually nothing (even telling them things that you shouldn't know can potentially pass, if you could have discovered them with other means, or even as great emphaty).<br /> <br /> When not only I, but also two other people accused you about being a HOP killjoy, you should ponder that, perhaps, you're not explaining things clearly. Instead of saying things like &quot;Please cite for me any time a sniper has fired a rifle and killed someone 500 miles away&quot;, which implies the potential observer having knowledge of the amount of miles that the bullet traveled, which imples knowing not only where it did impact but also where the soot came from and having perceived the lenght of the entire trajectory of the bullet (which would give the HAP Correspondence 2 senses that allow to sense &quot;all space&quot;), you could stick to &quot;there's no way in hell that an observer placed where the bullet disappears would not notice the sudden interruption of the sonic boom&quot;, that's a perfectly good HAP argument, even if some people may not agree with you about people realizing what happened, or the magnitude and importance of such realization.<br /> <br /> The argument of the observer expecting the bullet to hit something isn't so good because it implies that the observer knows there was a shoot and/or saw the bullet. Which doesn't need to be the case if the bullet was teleported far from where it would have naturally impacted. HAP can't know simultaneously that a bullet was shoot, a bullet disappeared and that a bullet should have impacted if there's distance between these phenomena, because, unlike HOP, he isn't all seeing. Of course, the secondof the three it's enough to make the whole thing Vulgar (if you agree with this argument).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to magically kill someone and create the injury and evidence of a bullet wound... that's a very different thing than actually sniping someone with Correspondence from a different city. Which would be an actual comparison to the coin trick in concept even if not in Sphere's used. </div> </div> </div>That's very interesting idea<br /> <br /> I can see that working for a bizarre magical gun-user of some kind. Perhaps shooting a largue voodoo doll or a target with a picture of your foe on your side of the planet, causing that (with Corr 3/Matter 3/Forces 3/ Prime 2) the person represented by the doll &quot;get's shoot&quot; (trough you would still have to deal with the fact that bullets do not &quot;appear&quot; from nowhere, and the hypotetical observer should expect to hear a sonic boom and all that shit, again, if we use your arguments, of course. But you can do that if the bullet comes from somewhere a sniper could potentially be, assuming total cover and no one in there)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Explain why teleportation sniping is Coincidental, but I can't use Correspondence to transmute a bullet into a dog mid teleportation to have a dog appear out of nowhere in an alley next to someone for whatever reason I have to do so (dogs live in alleys!). </div> </div> </div>Ironically, it seems that the dog isn't the problem here, as dogs do not produce sonic booms and no one would blink if they saw the dog appear from a small box in an alley. Transmuting a dog mid teleportation in a flying bullet may be simpler to pass as &quot;Coincidental&quot; under these assumptions <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, going back to my Cliffs of Dover example, from the top of the cliffs, you're not going to see or hear the rock splash into the water. That doesn't mean the HAPs wouldn't find it impossible for a rock to hit the water without sound or splash. </div> </div> </div>But what if the teleport happens <i>after </i>it splashes, and the water it's muddy...and then it teleports 500 miles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-30-2017, 12:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:41:52-07:00","id":1135487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135468#post1135468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is... basically missing the whole point I made about privately own guns (extremely restricted in China) vs. state owned guns. China have ~1.5 million active ground soldiers (that's not their whole military... that's just their people that fight on the ground), and ~1.5 million members of their armed police force (again, distinct from the larger police and state security forces); yes there is (probably China doesn't exactly publish much about this) a good amount of feeding from one into the other, but those are their official numbers for &quot;at a give time.&quot; So despite China's highly restrictive gun laws leading to very low private ownership rates.. there's a lot of people in China that know how to shoot.<br /> <br /> Strict gun laws also don't directly correlate to gun ownership rates (even if they decrease the US's uniquely weird distribution issues); though quantifying the strictness of gun laws is tricky to do an actual correlation with. Lots of EU countries (the EU has strong gun laws as part of membership in general, on top of any local restrictions which are common) have relatively high numbers of civilian guns. Canada and Australia are up there too. There are countries where guns are just outright banned too, but for the most part private gun ownership is more culturally linked than legally linked (though they do play into each other over a long enough period; Japan's gun laws are so strong banning private ownership would barely have an impact but gun bans are so old there's no gun culture like there are in lots of European/Western countries where people will jump through the hoops anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div> Considering China has a population of over a billion, I consider said soldiers rather uncompelling numbers. While 1.5 million (or 2-2.5, depending on the considered overlap you want to consider between soldiers/police) is a lot of people generally, it is small in the grand scheme. The state adds numbers, but not nearly enough to make it an average.<br /> <br /> I will agree strict gun laws don't necessarily correlate, though the entire worldwide numbers of gun ownership and experience/exposure are hard to get concretely, especially with the dark stats that abound. But seeing as even in America (the country with the most guns out there) ownership is 30%, and not even a big majority of those owners often use there guns (52% sometimes or often shooting at a range and 34% sometimes or often going hunting - noting that the remainder identify as either rarely or never), even if we're adding in non-owners who go to the range/borrower guns (couldn't really find concrete numbers on that) I'm just not seeing it really add up to the average. And as I get to noting further on, I'm not sure it is even a given that those with some experience would necessarily notice the difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, for clarity's sake, I'm drawing my stats from this survey. <a href=\"http://www.pewsocialtrends.org/2017/06/22/americas-complex-relationship-with-guns/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.pewsocialtrends.org/2017/...hip-with-guns/</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wait, didn't you just say anecdotes aren't helpful, and I responded by not continuing with anecdotes? </div> </div> </div> Anecdotes aren't helpful for laying out trends and the like. We're discussing two things now, essentially. The first being how many people have experience around guns (which would generally indicate what the average would be in identifying the sound difference we're discussing). The second point I'm getting at is whether those with experience even have the general ability to offhandedly recognize the sound difference in question (with the closest comparison being a normal shot versus a blank). I say offhandedly because this discussion is about noticing it as compared to being able to identify in a test.<br /> <br /> I mentioned it because I was contesting the concept you presented - that the only experience necessary to recognize the sound difference was 'You need to have spent a few hours at a range just hearing things, or gone on a few hunting trips.' I can't personally contest that because I haven't had those experiences, so I took it for granted, as was Aleph. But given I know someone who has gone on quite a number of hunting trips who claims they wouldn't be able to tell the difference without prompting, I have to question the claim that base that the experience you mention is enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's worth noting that the vast majority of this thread is basically arguing over whether bullets in flight are an observable phenomenon by &quot;average&quot; people, which is why the distribution thing comes up. Even if people stop arguing that bullets aren't observable (I kind of hope after posting a url for a video showing real time visible bullet air distortion this is somewhat put to rest), the argument then moves to can an &quot;average&quot; person see them and recognize that something weird (like the teleportation of the bullet) occurred. Because it if isn't &quot;average&quot; then I'm not applying HAP, but HOP. </div> </div> </div> As you will. I think you (or someone, not sure) noted it earlier anyway, the entire concept could be more easily pursuing other avenues while still being a magic sniper guy as well. But I just contest the idea of what the average person could tell here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 08-30-2017, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:42:38-07:00","id":1135548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135474#post1135474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I don't know, the statistics and facts are there to determine if it's observable &quot;by any person arround&quot; or not. There can be debate over if someting it's observable or not. It's important to understand why this is a thing in order to use it where you don't have things like &quot;pockets&quot;, or &quot;open spaces&quot;, but do have comparable situations. But I appreciate your common sense. It's what you need to use &quot;on the fly&quot; when you are playing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even when the bullet vanishing is not vulgar, the fact that another person drops dead somewhere in the world because of a random stray bullet shouldn't be. Where does it come from? It's illogical for a HAP to just accept this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T14:13:16-07:00","id":1135593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135474#post1135474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what's most important, in my opinion, if bullets in flight (and it's hypotetical vanishment) are an observable phenomenon by &quot;average&quot; people.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... do you have any thoughts given the video I tried to link to? Or looking at other bullet trace videos? You know, that anyone can watch and see the bullet's wake in flight?<br /> <br /> Nobody's really... well addressed me putting that out there. You can see bullet air wake. You can get a very good idea of how big an impact higher powered rifles leave when the bullet strikes something (the impact dust plumes are extremely easy to see from hundreds of feet away), and that video's maker even managed to briefly capture the bullet leaving the gun through a stroke of luck with lighting. As noted in the video the bullet is visible for all of four frames, but it's four frames where anyone can see a high powered bullet mid-flight. &quot;Average&quot; really shouldn't be in question for anything in that video.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the rote so powerful, though? </div> </div> </div>I actually don't think it is. It's a lot of work for an end result that could be done without it. In M20, I'd take the 1 Paradox point unless this is something I do a lot (any if you're magic sniping people more than once every two weeks for that Paradox to go away on its own... you have bigger problems). There are exceedingly better choices out there as long as they don't run too afoul of your Focus.<br /> <br /> The only issue I could see is if someone is using the Revised Jhor rules, where killing people directly with magic is supposed build up Resonance quickly that leads to Jhor. Thus the Euthanatos militant factions train extensively on mundane methods of killing to avoid that. In that understanding of things, anything that lets you Coincidentally kill someone with a mundane tool magically enhanced is a major benefit over the aneurysm style method.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When not only I, but also two other people accused you about being a HOP killjoy, you should ponder that, perhaps, you're not explaining things clearly. </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I think it's also fair to point out that at least two of you are making arguments (that we all agree on) that were getting labelled as HOP killjoy arguments on a different thread.<br /> <br /> The whole, &quot;That's HOP talking, not HAP!&quot; is basically, not a useful thing to throw around unless you really want to get into nitty gritty details. It too often just means, &quot;We disagree.&quot;<br /> <br /> It might not always be the best for clarity, but I also tend to say things in different ways when talking about the same topic because just repeating the same phrasing over and over is frustration building, and generally trying a dozen ways of saying something instead of one way a dozen times usually lets people hone in better on my intended meaning faster.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The argument of the observer expecting the bullet to hit something isn't so good because it implies that the observer knows there was a shoot and/or saw the bullet. Which doesn't need to be the case if the bullet was teleported far from where it would have naturally impacted. </div> </div> </div>But the whole point of the HAP/HOP is that they are focused on what's going on. The HAP knows there was a shot and/or sees the bullet because that's their job in this scenario. If they don't, they're not observing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HAP can't know simultaneously that a bullet was shoot, a bullet disappeared and that a bullet should have impacted if there's distance between these phenomena, because, unlike HOP, he isn't all seeing. Of course, the secondof the three it's enough to make the whole thing Vulgar (if you agree with this argument). </div> </div> </div>But the distance doesn't factor in. The HAP knows the bullet was shot (that has to be the case), assuming the bullet is observable they observe it disappearing, and they know the bullet should have impacted because that should happen as a matter of course (everyone believes that bullets fall down and hit something eventually). He doesn't need to be all seeing to know the bullet should land somewhere.<br /> <br /> If the bullet should be traveling so far that the HAP can't see both the spot of teleportation and the spot of impact without teleportation, that means putting the teleportation as close to the shooter as possible. This only makes the lack of sensory evidence of the bullet that much more noticeable to the HAP.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (trough you would still have to deal with the fact that bullets do not &quot;appear&quot; from nowhere, and the hypotetical observer should expect to hear a sonic boom and all that shit, again, if we use your arguments, of course. But you can do that if the bullet comes from somewhere a sniper could potentially be, assuming total cover and no one in there) </div> </div> </div>If you're already using forces, the sounds aren't that hard to make happen.<br /> <br /> The issue is mostly setting up the &quot;pocket&quot; as you note. Though it's not impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But what if the teleport happens <i>after </i>it splashes, and the water it's muddy...and then it teleports 500 miles. </div> </div> </div>A wet rock appears out of thin air 500 miles away in a very vulgar fashion. This goes back to the whole issue of inertia I brought up earlier. If you assume the rock continues moving with it's pre-teleportation velocity, that's gone from &quot;really fast as it plummets into the water&quot; to &quot;really slow as the impact with the water absorbs a huge amount of that force.&quot; Any disagreement over something fast moving being observable or not doesn't matter if the thing is now barely moving at all.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T15:23:23-07:00","id":1135959,"title":"","content":"I didn't see the specific video you tried to link to, but from what I can tell, bullet traces actually require special scopes to see rather than being noticeable with the naked eye? And even then, it's a blink and you miss it slight distortion of the air.<br /> <br /> Someone who's spotting bullet traces with the naked eye or using specialized equipment is not an 'average' observer. Thus negating the whole argument. I specifically characterized your arguments as Hypothetical Omniscient Observer, not because you were full in, but because you were in essence arguing there are 'average' observers at every step along the process that might possibly break the illusion. To paraphrase Aleph, putting the observer in the mages pocket.<br /> <br /> It's possible to explain BOTH events caused by the magic. The bullet dissapearing, &quot;You just blinked dude. It's no big deal you missed it.&quot; And the Bullet Appearing again. &quot;A sniper! We're taking fire, get under cover if you don't want to end up like Bobby!&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead you're assuming that there is a forensic technician or a practiced marksman standing at the exact point that it disappears, primed for disbelief.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T17:09:12-07:00","id":1136000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1135959#post1135959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't see the specific video you tried to link to, but from what I can tell, bullet traces actually require special scopes to see rather than being noticeable with the naked eye? And even then, it's a blink and you miss it slight distortion of the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to reliably and clearly capture bullet traces, you want a specialized camera set up (but that's true of pretty much every sensory input compared to human senses).<br /> <br /> However you don't need them to see them; especially for supersonic rounds.<br /> <br /> &quot;Blink if you miss it,&quot; should be irrelevant to HAP. The whole point of a HAP is that they'd see things even if nobody is actually looking. HAPs don't blink at just the right time to miss the effect. This is not a viable standard to hold to. If a HAP is subject to blinking at the perfect moment to miss things, how can the HAP see anything that only takes a moment to occur? &quot;I summon a gun into my hand.&quot; &quot;That's vulgar.&quot; &quot;No, the HAP blinks for while the gun appears there, so they just assume I pulled it out while they weren't looking.&quot; That's not functional.<br /> <br /> Either something is visible, and the HAP sees it, or it's not and they don't. If you start subjecting HAPs to things like &quot;blinking&quot; then you're just throwing the concept of HAP out the window.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone who's spotting bullet traces with the naked eye or using specialized equipment is not an 'average' observer. </div> </div> </div>Based on... what?<br /> <br /> I post the url for a video shot with a normal camera with bullet traces clearly visible on it... and you kinda think that's not the case, so it's not the case? That's not really how reasonable discussion works. If you want to cite something about bullet trace viewing, please do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I specifically characterized your arguments as Hypothetical Omniscient Observer, not because you were full in, but because you were in essence arguing there are 'average' observers at every step along the process that might possibly break the illusion. </div> </div> </div>I was in essence, never arguing this in the slightest. I referenced three specific locations, and placing in general (since the HAP is placed where best to view the effect, not in a set location like 5 feet behind the mage).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To paraphrase Aleph, putting the observer in the mages pocket. </div> </div> </div>To paraphrase:<br /> <br /> You are in essence arguing that vulgar magic never occurs because open air is the same as being in a mage's pocket because average senses for a HAP are &quot;can't sense anything ever.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yep. &quot;HOP&quot; is still clearing intending to mean, &quot;I invoke this to win the Internet without having to address what you say!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You just blinked dude. It's no big deal you missed it.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's vulgar without witnesses, not coincidental.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead you're assuming that there is a forensic technician or a practiced marksman standing at the exact point that it disappears, primed for disbelief. </div> </div> </div>No... you're just lying about what I've said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T17:24:18-07:00","id":1136008,"title":"","content":"And you seem to be using the Strawman fallacy as YOUR get out of arguing free card. By entirely mischaracterizing my argument, and then claiming I'm mischaracterizing yours by your significantly altered reading of mine, you expect me to roll over.<br /> <br /> Everything I saw said that you CAN see them without the scope, but it was difficult. And every video I saw WITHOUT the scope, the effect wasn't actually visible. Or at least I couldn't see it.<br /> <br /> A small, fast moving object is not something that is easy to see. Whether it is in the open air or not. <i>I have worked at a golf course.</i> You could fill a house with the number of <i>brightly colored neon balls</i> that people lose track of at significantly slower speeds. People lose track of small moving objects. It happens. All the time. By ignoring this and focusing on the 'it's in the open air' like everything that's in the open air is clearly visible regardless of literally every other factor. You don't need to actually physically block something to prevent it from being seen. And the assertion that you do is patently ridiculous.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Hypothetical Average Observer&quot; stands next to the mage. Or next to the target of the effect. It's a 'hypothetical bystander who's RIGHT THERE witnessing you do magic. It is not someone looking down your coat sleeve. the Hypothetical Average Observer is your Audience.<br /> <br /> And I never said they didn't actually witness it. But you can't see a moving bullet unless intently looking for it. The Hypothetical Average Observer is just a guy or gal that's there. Not there SPECIFICALLY WATCHING for anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T22:12:46-07:00","id":1136089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136008#post1136008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you seem to be using the Strawman fallacy as YOUR get out of arguing free card.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I got caught using a strawman, so I'm just going to call the other guy guilt of it!&quot; isn't really a good look man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything I saw said that you CAN see them without the scope, but it was difficult. </div> </div> </div>So.... my strawman that I claimed you said you can't see them without the scope?<br /> <br /> Please quote that. Because I'm looking at my own damned words, and that's not in there.<br /> <br /> This would all go better if you stopped claiming/implying I said things I haven't said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And every video I saw WITHOUT the scope, the effect wasn't actually visible. Or at least I couldn't see it. </div> </div> </div>OK, first, cite something? Because the video I posted the url for isn't using any special optics for the camera and you can see it in all the shots. It's a hell of a lot harder than videos setup with optics, but it's there. Also, you do realize the the &quot;scope&quot; here is just a normal rifle or spotter scope, right? It's magnification so you get see more detail, and for the real pretty videos they adjust the focus a bit to highlight the trace. It's not specific technology for that purpose, it's just scopes people firing long range are already using.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A small, fast moving object is not something that is easy to see. </div> </div> </div>Which is why we're talking about things like trace and the sonic boom a supersonic bullet creates. Those are more obvious elements that last longer and are easier to observe than the bullet itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> People lose track of small moving objects. </div> </div> </div>Which was... the exact same argument as to why people can disappear in a crowd. &quot;People lose track of people in a crowd all the time, so the HAP doesn't notice and loses track and teleporting/invisibility/etc. are missed.&quot; If we all agree that's a bad argument, how is this any different?<br /> <br /> I can list dozens of reasons why people miss things. But it HAP is subject to all of them all the time, the HAP stops being a useful device. It just turns into table arguments over if the HAP blinked or got the sun in their eyes, or whatever BS to claim that the HAP loses track of what's going on.<br /> <br /> Does the HAP miss things if the lights are off? Can a naked mage standing in a room turn off the lights and conjure clothing on and the HAP is fooled by the lights being off? Or is the HAP not fooled by such things because seeing someone summon clothing out of nothing is clearly vulgar and the darkness can remove witnesses at best?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;Hypothetical Average Observer&quot; stands next to the mage. Or next to the target of the effect. </div> </div> </div>Citation please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a 'hypothetical bystander who's RIGHT THERE witnessing you do magic. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Hypothetical Average Observer is just a guy or gal that's there. Not there SPECIFICALLY WATCHING for anything. </div> </div> </div>Pick one. You're arguing two different things. Either the HAP is actively witnessing what you're doing, or they're not specifically watching. It can't be both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 09-01-2017, 01:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T04:48:33-07:00","id":1136141,"title":"","content":"A note: I agree with Heavy Arms that the HAP is not just standing next to the mage. The HAP is everywhere an observer might possibly be, for realistic reasons. That is, an observer won't be inside your tiny Magic Box when you do a stage trick vanishing act, or inside your pocket, but an observer would be in every part of the alley you're in, every corner of your room, your shower cabin (oh murr), etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136089#post1136089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the HAP miss things if the lights are off?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a FYI; according to, of all the books, HDYDT...yes, that can happen. See &quot;The Batman&quot; on page 77 (Also referenced on page73 in BoS), and the explanation of teleportation higher on the page..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nix vanishes right in front of people = vulgar with witnesses.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nix ducks into the darkness and disappears = coincidental.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Nix jumps out a window in broad daylight; no one sees<br /> Nix on the other side of that window, but if someone<br /> did, then they\u2019d see Nix vanish = vulgar without witnesses.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a confounding amount of wiggle-room in such<br /> situations, and the Storyteller has the ultimate right to decide<br /> where vulgar magick ends and coincidence begins. </div> </div> </div>It explicitely makes use of a visually hard to observe environment from one which could realistically appear or disappear mundanely in the eyes of others.<br /> <br /> As always, circumstance and realism play a role - if you stand in a room, the light turns off and on, and you are standing there with clothes...well. That wouldn't fly. Nor would it if there is no way you could have hidden the clothes in the room before, ahem, 'dressing' in them. Or if you were frisked before pulling out the mystery handcannon from your coat.<br /> <br /> It's essentially a play of make-believe in front of actual and invisible observers with mundane senses alike. The same kind of make-believe that pulling the non-existant credit card out of your pocket is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-01-2017, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:08:51-07:00","id":1136205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A note: I agree with Heavy Arms that the HAP is not just standing next to the mage.<b> The HAP is everywhere an observer might possibly be, for realistic reasons. </b>That is, an observer<b> won't be inside your tiny Magic Box when you do a stage trick vanishing act</b>, or inside your pocket, <b>but an observer would be in every part of the alley you're in, every corner of your room,</b> your shower cabin (oh murr), etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would add that the Observer can be anywhere...but not perceive everywhere simultaneously. HAP can't compare notes between what any other being would perceive as isolated events. Otherwise, the observer would be both seeing the Batman jumping into the night, and just bellow the window, expecting the Batman to fall on top of his hypotetical body (can sense with tact, knows where the Batman jumped).<br /> <br /> I take the HAP not as a being with invisibility and co-location superpowers, <i>but <u>as a question</u>: </i><b>If there was a normal person <i>anywhere</i>, would that person count as Witness?</b>, which, I think it's very different from: <b>If there was a normal person <i>everywhere</i>, would that person count as Witness?</b>.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm not saying that the HAP it's not somewhere, nor that it can't be very attentive. HAP it's in China and in US, but can't correlate a fact from China with a fact from US. <i>B</i>eing able to perceive and understand simultaneously <i>all of space and time</i> it's far from what an average observer can hypotetically acomplish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... do you have any thoughts given the video I tried to link to? Or looking at other bullet trace videos? You know, that anyone can watch and see the bullet's wake in flight?</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, it should be Vulgar with two exeptions:<br /> <br /> If there's very poor visibility AND the mage uses Forces to make up for the loss of the sound (I'm still unconvinced that the Observer should know where the bullet it's going to fall, between how hard was to follow those bullets in the video, the chance of they being deviated by wind, and the skill of snipers in producing seeminly impossible angles)<br /> <br /> In the center of zone where there's good security and few people ever heard a gunshot (much less saw one). Countries where law forbiddes the use of weapons (and where law it's actualy obeyed to an extent) may count. This it's to take in count Monalfie's argument (US IT'S very good toothing, and I don't know more than one person that ever fired a gun) but at the same time I'm unconvinced if the number of people that knows this reaches the point where it's common knowledge everywhere or not, thus shoveling it into Reality Zones seems like it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-01-2017, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:30:07-07:00","id":1136214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136141#post1136141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a FYI; according to, of all the books, HDYDT...yes, that can happen. See &quot;The Batman&quot; on page 77 (Also referenced on page73 in BoS), and the explanation of teleportation higher on the page.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Batman&quot; has limitations. You can't Batman across the city in one effect, the HAP might buy you ducking into a dark alley and appearing a block away in another dark alley a few moments later, but not across a mile in a span of time nobody could reasonably travel one. The Batman also requires Forces, not just normal darkness, to pull off. Basically, this trick is inherently limited to a distance that would be believably traveled, even if you're actually teleporting around, and magical sensory illusions to be convincing enough to pull off. That actually bolsters my point about the sniper issue. For all the people saying that noticing traveling impossible distances is HOP, not HAP, &quot;The Batman&quot; entry objectively disagrees (emphasis mine): &quot;So long as no one could actually witness him disappearing in some impossible way, or <u>moving from one place to another in a fashion that cannot be explained by conventional physics</u> (like appearing at the other side of a bridge without crossing through the intervening space), this trick may remain coincidental.&quot;<br /> <br /> You also skipped the part in the stuff above that which says:<br /> &quot;\u2022 If the mage disappears into darkness (see The Batman, below), and the witness would have reason to believe she could have gone somewhere else, then it\u2019s probably coincidental.<br /> \u2022 And if the mage goes somewhere and then vanishes, but nobody sees her vanish, then it\u2019s probably vulgar without witnesses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is very relevant to putting the Nix examples you cited into context. &quot;The witness would have reason to believe she could have gone somewhere else,&quot; is vital to anything like &quot;Nix ducks into the darkness and disappears.&quot; The text requires this to both remain within the reasonable amount of distance a person could travel, and the darkness does not eliminate the need for the teleportation to look possible if the lights come back on.<br /> <br /> If you're in a hermetically sealed room, darkness doesn't help you any more, because there needs to be the belief that you could have moved the distance without magic.<br /> <br /> The only consistent way to rectify all of this is to treat the HAP as seeing what it needs to see to judge the effect. The HAP notices a window you could have left through even if there's no light to see you or the window, because seeing the window is needed to judge the effect. The difference between HAP and HOP, is the HAP stops at noticing there's a believable way for you to have escaped through the window, where the HOP sees you teleport instead of using it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As always, circumstance and realism play a role... </div> </div> </div>Yep. Which has always been at the core of my argument. There's nothing hiding the sensory information of the rifle shot pre-teleportation (and it's incredibly hard to do so in general with high powered rifles). Setting up a circumstance where you don't give yourself away is at a minimum incredibly difficult, mostly due to the distances and forces involved. Dampening trace and sound would make the bullet disappearing more believable (though I still take issue with the bullet never hitting anything being something the HAP just misses) to a HAP downrange, but less believable to a HAP next to the shooter. And realism I've brought of a few times with things like, &quot;you can't shoot someone 500 miles away,&quot; which I consider analogous to, &quot;you can't Batman across a major urban bridge in 3 seconds.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T09:41:26-07:00","id":1136218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136205#post1136205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify, I'm not saying that the HAP it's not somewhere, nor that it can't be very attentive. HAP it's in China and in US, but can't correlate a fact from China with a fact from US. <i>B</i>eing able to perceive and understand simultaneously <i>all of space and time</i> it's far from what an average observer can hypotetically acomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>HDYDT does somewhat address this by saying that teleportation and similar things push up against the metaphysical weight of Consensus and ripple reality in a way that is apparently felt by HAPs. I don't particularly like this explanation, but it's in there.<br /> <br /> And nobody's asking for the HAP to perceive all of space and time, just the tiny portions of it necessary to judge a magical effect.<br /> <br /> Or another way to see it, I'd rather HAPs be &quot;joined&quot; by Correspondence or Time magic to be on both ends of an effect, than HDYDT's &quot;notable ripple in reality&quot; bit. The whole idea of a reality ripple from teleportation that HAPs can feel just seems to completely run contrary to how things are described as working.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my opinion, it should be Vulgar with two exeptions: </div> </div> </div>Seems reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:35:00-07:00","id":1136246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136214#post1136214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also skipped the part in the stuff above that which says:<br /> &quot;\u2022 If the mage disappears into darkness (see The Batman, below), and the witness would have reason to believe she could have gone somewhere else, then it\u2019s probably coincidental.<br /> \u2022 And if the mage goes somewhere and then vanishes, but nobody sees her vanish, then it\u2019s probably vulgar without witnesses.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is very relevant to putting the Nix examples you cited into context. &quot;The witness would have reason to believe she could have gone somewhere else,&quot; is vital to anything like &quot;Nix ducks into the darkness and disappears.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite!<br /> It's why I said &quot;It explicitely makes use of a visually hard to observe environment <i>from one which could realistically appear or disappear mundanely in the eyes of others.</i>&quot; and &quot;As always, <i>circumstance and realism</i> play a role,&quot; with the examples given afterwards, and the whole spiel about realistic 'make-believe'.<br /> <br /> I think I tried to stress that well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T10:43:52-07:00","id":1136252,"title":"","content":"OK. When you responded to my question with &quot;yes&quot; it felt a bit different in intention.<br /> <br /> Basically, darkness doesn't inherently fool the HAP by itself, but darkness can certainly push the HAP's conclusion towards coincidental taking into account all the other factors. Agreed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T11:16:58-07:00","id":1136268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136252#post1136252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK. When you responded to my question with &quot;yes&quot; it felt a bit different in intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happens <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't worry about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136252#post1136252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, darkness doesn't inherently fool the HAP by itself, but darkness can certainly push the HAP's conclusion towards coincidental taking into account all the other factors. Agreed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T16:50:02-07:00","id":1136438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136089#post1136089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;I got caught using a strawman, so I'm just going to call the other guy guilt of it!&quot; isn't really a good look man.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So.... my strawman that I claimed you said you can't see them without the scope?<br /> <br /> Please quote that. Because I'm looking at my own damned words, and that's not in there.<br /> <br /> This would all go better if you stopped claiming/implying I said things I haven't said.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> OK, first, cite something? Because the video I posted the url for isn't using any special optics for the camera and you can see it in all the shots. It's a hell of a lot harder than videos setup with optics, but it's there. Also, you do realize the the &quot;scope&quot; here is just a normal rifle or spotter scope, right? It's magnification so you get see more detail, and for the real pretty videos they adjust the focus a bit to highlight the trace. It's not specific technology for that purpose, it's just scopes people firing long range are already using.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which is why we're talking about things like trace and the sonic boom a supersonic bullet creates. Those are more obvious elements that last longer and are easier to observe than the bullet itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which was... the exact same argument as to why people can disappear in a crowd. &quot;People lose track of people in a crowd all the time, so the HAP doesn't notice and loses track and teleporting/invisibility/etc. are missed.&quot; If we all agree that's a bad argument, how is this any different?<br /> <br /> I can list dozens of reasons why people miss things. But it HAP is subject to all of them all the time, the HAP stops being a useful device. It just turns into table arguments over if the HAP blinked or got the sun in their eyes, or whatever BS to claim that the HAP loses track of what's going on.<br /> <br /> Does the HAP miss things if the lights are off? Can a naked mage standing in a room turn off the lights and conjure clothing on and the HAP is fooled by the lights being off? Or is the HAP not fooled by such things because seeing someone summon clothing out of nothing is clearly vulgar and the darkness can remove witnesses at best.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Pick one. You're arguing two different things. Either the HAP is actively witnessing what you're doing, or they're not specifically watching. It can't be both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your strawman is claiming that I'm accusing you of HOP because I'm losing the argument. I'm claiming you're using HOP because you are bordering on HOP because &quot;Thousands of HAP's using Specialized gear watching every step of the process like a hawk&quot; while not quite 'one observer who knows everything' is practically the same for all intents and purposes.<br /> <br /> AND WHO, aside from your hypothetical forensic technician made up wholecloth to defeat coincidence, CARRIES A SNIPER SCOPE WHILE WALKING DOWN THE STREET?! And even more so, who uses it to spot a bullet traveling along a path they don't anticipate it to be going down?<br /> <br /> I still haven't SEEN this video you posted because I searched through the thread and couldn't find it. I googled Bullet Traces independently, and watched two videos, one WITH a scope, where it was barely visible, and one without, where it wasn't visible at all except as a slight distortion as the bullet hit the target.<br /> <br /> Small fast moving objects do not require outside intervention to lose track of. they require ACTIVE dedicated attention to NOT lose track of. The default here is not 'you maintain track of the small quickly moving object' the default here is 'you LOSE track of the small quickly moving object.' I know I'D ask for a perception roll, possibly at diff 8-9 to spot a bullet in flight without expecting it coming.<br /> <br /> If the mage is in a closet? Yes. the point of HAP is not what they do or do not see, and seeing it as such is what makes it pointless. The point of HAP is &quot;Could I bullshit this? Or would the average person see these events as clearly impossible?&quot; Putting on clothes, losing track of a bullet or hell, teleporting from one shadow in cleveland to another shadow in Shang-Hai....<br /> <br /> Is it? The HAP is there, in a manner in which they can watch what you do. But they are not ACTIVELY watching you. They are a hypothetical bystander. Not your mother.<br /> <br /> Also, asking for citations when discussing logic. Nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T18:28:54-07:00","id":1136471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1133616-remote-sniper-rote?p=1136438#post1136438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your strawman is claiming that I'm accusing you of HOP because I'm losing the argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I agreed that you weren't, it would be a fallacy fallacy (I'd be dismissing your conclusions because I consider the logic false, even though false logic doesn't mean the conclusion can't be correct anyway), not a strawman; with a splash of ad hominem phrasing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm claiming you're using HOP because you are bordering on HOP because &quot;Thousands of HAP's using Specialized gear watching every step of the process like a hawk&quot; while not quite 'one observer who knows everything' is practically the same for all intents and purposes. </div> </div> </div>See, this is a strawman, because I never used &quot;thousands of HAP's using specialized gear watching every step of the process&quot; in any of my arguments. You invented this and are assigning it to me to argue against. So... yeah. Not really buying that you get how these things work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I still haven't SEEN this video you posted because I searched through the thread and couldn't find it. </div> </div> </div>I screwed up the forum code (as I've said before) and ended up posting the url as raw text, not a link or embeded video. You are not giving my increased confidence that you're actually reading what I'm saying if you can't find a url with [url] tags around it in my post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point of HAP is &quot;Could I bullshit this? Or would the average person see these events as clearly impossible?&quot; </div> </div> </div>Right. The average person seeing <b>these events</b> would not believe them as possible. Nobody believes shooting someone 500 miles away with a rifle is possible. There's no way to actually bullshit the total events. The whole argument for making it coincidental is that you can bullshit enough of the individual pieces that it doesn't matter if the sum total doesn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they are not ACTIVELY watching you. </div> </div> </div>Citation please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, asking for citations when discussing logic. Nice. </div> </div> </div>I'm asking for a citation because you're making affirmative claims about something. Where is HAP defined as watching things the way you're claiming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}